{"level":30,"time":1776272524099,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LCNdFQ2sNwwBMdrt3Z8d28","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've read the grouping file. This is \"el-md-exp/1.md\" so my grouping ID is \"1\". Let me summarize what I understand:\n\n**Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**\n\nThis grouping covers clearance requirements between overhead electric distribution and transmission facilities and proposed site features (buildings, fences, walls, driveways, etc.).\n\n**Key regulatory points:**\n- 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead primary, neutral, and secondary conductors\n- 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n- 16 feet vertical clearance for driveways (parking without trucks)\n- 18 feet vertical clearance for roads/streets/areas with truck traffic\n- 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors for trees\n- 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors for trees\n- Clearances must be measured from outside conductor, NOT pole centerline\n- Distribution: <60kV (typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV)\n- Transmission: ≥60kV (69kV, 138kV, 345kV)\n\n**Checklist items:** 47 items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47)\n\nNow I need to:\n\n1. **Check Applicability**: Does this project have overhead electric facilities? I need to check the facts.md file and understand the site conditions.\n\n2. **Research Phase**: Review the site plan to understand where overhead electric facilities are located, what features are proposed, and whether there are any clearance issues.\n\n3. **Evaluate Each Item**: Go through all 47 checklist items and determine which are applicable and which ones have failures.\n\n4. **Return Findings**: Output only the fail and not-verifiable items in structured format.\n\