{"level":30,"time":1776272527978,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01EvxaSvnwbduGhhUm4pADYd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have key information:\n\nFrom facts.md, I can see:\n- **Easements that may be relevant**: \n  - Two 5' Electric Easements (plat-dedicated, TravisCounty Doc 73/76, Case C8S-75-160)\n  - 7.5' Public Utility Easement (plat-dedicated)\n  - These are DEDICATED and noted as existing\n\nThis is critical: The site has ELECTRIC EASEMENTS. This means there may be existing or planned overhead electric facilities.\n\n**Applicability Assessment:**\nThe grouping covers clearance requirements from overhead electric lines. The facts.md mentions electric easements exist on the property, but I need to verify:\n1. Whether there are ACTUAL overhead electric facilities (poles, conductors, lines) on or adjacent to the site\n2. What the site plan shows regarding these facilities\n\nLet me check the site plan sheets, particularly:\n- Sheet 1 (Cover) - might have location map\n- Sheet 3 (General Notes) - might mention utilities\n- Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) - shows existing infrastructure\n- Sheet 9 (Site Plan) - shows all site features\n- Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) - most relevant!\n\nLet me start by checking Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) to see what overhead electric facilities exist.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8483,"cache_read_input_tokens":30902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8483},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa426fab-05eb-4a3a-b7ff-045b4f6