{"level":30,"time":1776272529433,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011pYPuz8J4VuqRnmZesAyhT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 4 — Existing Conditions Survey\n     2→\n     3→Topographic survey detailing existing structures, trees, and property boundaries.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Boundary, Improvements, Topographic & Tree Survey representing the existing conditions for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to document the baseline physical state of the site prior to development, detailing topographic contours, existing structures, property boundaries, easements, and a comprehensive tree inventory.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Existing Slab Finished Floor Elevation (F.F.E.): 686.8\n    11→* Survey Coordinate System: Texas Coordinate System of 1983 (NAD83) Central Zone, Grid\n    12→* Largest surveyed trees on site: 36\" Hackberry (Tree #4028), 34\" Live Oak (Tree #4042), and 28\" Live Oaks/Hackberry (Trees #4000, #4025, #4026)\n    13→* Job Number: 20240953 \n    14→* Project Number: RJ3 70496\n    15→\n    16→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    17→\n    18→* **Block 1**: Main site plan drawing — Shows the existing property conditions including topographic contours, property lines, existing slabs, fences, utility lines, and surveyed tree locations (marked with '+' and ID numbers). Notable areas include \"LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION\" and adjacent \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, topographic contours, and physical site features.\n    19→* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\n    20→* **Block 12**: Tree Table — A schedule listing the cataloged trees found on the property, detailing their ID number (corresponding to the plan drawing), caliper size in inches, and species (e.g., Live Oak, Hackberry, Pecan). READ for exact values and species of specific trees.\n    21→* **Blocks 2, 4, 10**: Project and Title Blocks — Contains the project name (Valley View Townhomes), site address, sheet title (Existing Conditions Survey), and contact information for Bleyl Engineering and Sinclair Land Surveying. READ for project context and firm details.\n    22→* **Blocks 3, 6, 8**: Survey Data & Document Control — Contains the survey's bearing basis (NAD83), job/project numbers, sheet numbering (Sheet 4 of 39), and CAD/design routing information. READ for specific coordinate system references and document tracking numbers.\n    23→* **Blocks 7, 9, 11**: Boilerplate & Administrative — Contains surveyor certification notes, the Registered Professional Land Surveyor (Ryan T. Lenz) signature and state seal, and a list of Bleyl Engineering office locations. READ the block content for surveyor credentials, certification dates, and legal disclaimers.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    28→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6450ffe4-612c-4eea-8b35-57aec9f3f591","uuid":"7292c05c-73a5-4048-880a-a6ea977e5331","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 4 — Existing Conditions Survey\n\nTopographic survey detailing existing structures, trees, and property boundaries.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Boundary, Improvements, Topographic & Tree Survey representing the existing conditions for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to document the baseline physical state of the site prior to development, detailing topographic contours, existing structures, property boundaries, easements, and a comprehensive tree inventory.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Existing Slab Finished Floor Elevation (F.F.E.): 686.8\n* Survey Coordinate System: Texas Coordinate System of 1983 (NAD83) Central Zone, Grid\n* Largest surveyed trees on site: 36\" Hackberry (Tree #4028), 34\" Live Oak (Tree #4042), and 28\" Live Oaks/Hackberry (Trees #4000, #4025, #4026)\n* Job Number: 20240953 \n* Project Number: RJ3 70496\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 1**: Main site plan drawing — Shows the existing property conditions including topographic contours, property lines, existing slabs, fences, utility lines, and surveyed tree locations (marked with '+' and ID numbers). Notable areas include \"LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION\" and adjacent \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, topographic contours, and physical site features.\n* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\n* **Block 12**: Tree Table — A schedule listing the cataloged trees found on the property, detailing their ID number (corresponding to the plan drawing), caliper size in inches, and species (e.g., Live Oak, Hackberry, Pecan). READ for exact values and species of specific trees.\n* **Blocks 2, 4, 10**: Project and Title Blocks — Contains the project name (Valley View Townhomes), site address, sheet title (Existing Conditions Survey), and contact information for Bleyl Engineering and Sinclair Land Surveying. READ for project context and firm details.\n* **Blocks 3, 6, 8**: Survey Data & Document Control — Contains the survey's bearing basis (NAD83), job/project numbers, sheet numbering (Sheet 4 of 39), and CAD/design routing information. READ for specific coordinate system references and document tracking numbers.\n* **Blocks 7, 9, 11**: Boilerplate & Administrative — Contains surveyor certification notes, the Registered Professional Land Surveyor (Ryan T. Lenz) signature and state seal, and a list of Bleyl Engineering office locations. READ the block content for surveyor credentials, certification dates, and legal disclaimers.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776272529500,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01F71tcLmX6w5Bu3K7kAzyep","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that the site plan includes:\n- Sheet 21: Preliminary Electrical Design Plan - This would show electrical infrastructure\n- Sheet 31: Landscape Plan - This would show trees\n- Sheet 35: Landscape Calculations - This would include plant lists\n\nNow let me look at the guides for these sheets to understand what's on them, starting with the electrical plan to determine if there are overhead lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3135,"cache_read_input_tokens":31773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3135},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3857099-05e9-4b26-b534-a07960b24bfd","uuid":"a8d0ba12-b51c-401f-9177-16091cc25f5f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272529503,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016pdvyS5VuPHLHubzMfvXGb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n     2→\n     3→Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    18→*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    19→*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n    20→*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n    22→*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n    23→*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    28→    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d155abec-404b-4144-83fe-2ada3fa35846","uuid":"04f1d438-562d-4df7-9b4d-a0229425536b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
