{"level":30,"time":1776272538544,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"This is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for a townhome project. I need to identify and analyze all transformer pads shown on this sheet. Please provide:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations:** Identify the exact location (by building or site area) of each transformer pad shown on the plan\n2. **Transformer Specifications:** What service types are shown (single-phase or three-phase), pad dimensions, and any AE Design detail callouts\n3. **Clearance Evidence:** For each transformer pad, identify:\n   - Clearance distance to buildings/structures\n   - Clearance distance to any fences or site features\n   - Access door orientation\n   - Any access area dimensions (hot-stick use areas)\n   - Positioning relative to utilities, trees, sidewalks, or parking areas\n   - Whether the pad is within any easements\n4. **Underground Utility Routing:** Show how electrical, water, wastewater, and storm drain lines are routed relative to each transformer pad\n5. **Equipment Details:** Are transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type, service phase) shown or referenced? Are bollard details shown?\n6. **Overall Site Layout:** Describe the general positioning of transformers within the site context\n\nPlease be specific about measurements, clearances, and exact locations visible on the plan.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272538654,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01M2Buujecqp2MnAMDxbUGiu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The legend shows key symbols including:\n- UTILITY POLE\n- LIGHT POLE\n- O.H.U.L. (OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE)\n- TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n\nThis confirms that the survey might show existing utility poles or overhead utility lines. The legend specifically lists \"UTILITY POLE\" and \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\" as symbols, which means they CAN be shown on the plan if they exist. Let me use the vision tool to check if Sheet 4 actually shows any existing overhead utility poles or lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2140,"cache_read_input_tokens":43908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2140},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa426fab-05eb-4a3a-b7ff-045b4f6362f9","uuid":"52ed3898-7a57-40b1-90b2-d05dd27b6320"}
