{"level":30,"time":1776272539263,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013PBjDma17oQXZf72RNoBJB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I found something very important:\n\nFrom Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan), Block 2: The site plan drawing shows:\n- \"Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and **overhead electric (OHE)**\"\n\nSo there IS overhead electric infrastructure shown on the landscape plan. Now I need to:\n\n1. Use the vision tool to examine Sheet 31 more closely to see:\n   - Exact location of the overhead electric lines\n   - What trees are shown on the landscape plan\n   - Distances between trees and overhead electric facilities\n\n2. Review the tree data from Sheet 32 to understand what species are proposed\n\n3. Check if there's a plant schedule that identifies tree species and their utility compatibility status\n\nLet me also check Sheet 35 which has landscape calculations and tree preservation notes, as that might have plant schedule information.\n\nBut first, let me use the vision tool to examine Sheet 31 in detail to understand the overhead electric situation and tree locations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2506,"cache_read_input_tokens":38964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2506},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d155abec-404b-4144-83fe-2ada3fa35846","uuid":"e0e8bac6-c93f-418c-8b38-5825c1c45353"}
