{"level":30,"time":1776272569160,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Review the existing conditions survey sheet carefully for any overhead electric utility poles, conductors, or overhead utility lines. Look for:\n1. Any symbols indicating utility poles (typically shown as circles with an X or similar symbol)\n2. Any overhead utility lines (shown as dashed lines with notations like \"O.H.U.L.\" or similar)\n3. Pole locations on the property or immediately adjacent to the property boundaries, especially along Valley View Road or at the property edges\n4. Any indication of electric easements or utility infrastructure\n\nAre there any overhead electric poles or conductors visible on this survey? If so, where are they located relative to the property boundaries?","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (4)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272575479,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"I need to understand the tree planting plan and its relationship to overhead electric infrastructure. Please identify: 1) Are overhead electric lines depicted on this landscape plan? If yes, describe their location (e.g., running along Valley View Road, through the property, etc.). 2) What tree symbols are shown (shade trees, ornamental trees) and their general locations on the site? 3) Are there any notes or dimensions showing clearances from trees to overhead electric infrastructure? 4) Which trees appear to be located near overhead electric lines or poles (within ~50 feet based on typical clearance requirements)? Be specific about tree locations relative to building names or site features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here is the information regarding the tree planting plan and overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n**1) Are overhead electric lines depicted on this landscape plan? If yes, describe their location.**\n*   **Yes**, overhead electric lines are depicted on the plan.\n*   A utility line labeled **\"-OHE-\"** (Overhead Electric) runs along the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the property shown in the plan.\n*   Additionally, along the left (western) boundary bordering \"Valley View Road\", there is a utility line labeled **\"-E-\"** that includes symbols resembling utility poles (circles with a dot or cross in the center) at regular intervals.\n\n**2) What tree symbols are shown (shade trees, ornamental trees) and their general locations on the site?**\nThe plan does not explicitly categorize trees as \"shade\" or \"ornamental\" in the provided key, but rather by their functional zoning purpose. Various circular tree symbols (some with internal crosshairs, 'x' marks, or smaller circles) are distributed across the site.\nBased on the **KEY NOTES** (bottom right), the following tree types/labels are identified:\n*   **\"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**: These are predominantly located in the prominent shaded area along the left boundary facing Valley View Road. Examples are labeled \"SY/M\" and are shown as large circle symbols with crosshairs.\n*   **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**: These are located within the internal parking areas, such as the islands and planters near the building footprint. An example is labeled \"PL/M\" near the center-top.\n*   **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**: Located along the top (northern) property boundary buffer.\n*   **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**: Scattered throughout the buffers, including the top edge, bottom edge, and right edge. Examples are shown as circles with an 'M' or 'M' alongside other designations.\n\n**3) Are there any notes or dimensions showing clearances from trees to overhead electric infrastructure?**\n*   **No**, there are no visible notes, dimensions, or specific callouts on this plan indicating required clearances between proposed trees and the overhead electric infrastructure.\n*   The text blocks provided (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\") do not contain any information regarding utility clearances.\n\n**4) Which trees appear to be located near overhead electric lines or poles (within ~50 feet based on typical clearance requirements)?**\nBased on the graphic scale provided (1\" = 20'-0\"), several trees are located well within 50 feet of the indicated electric lines:\n*   **Bottom Boundary (-OHE- line):** A row of newly proposed trees (indicated by circles with internal crosshairs or dots) is planted in the narrow landscape buffer between the bottom property line/OHE line and the adjacent drive aisle (labeled \"SD\"). These are planted in very close proximity to the line. Specifically, near the bottom right corner, there are trees explicitly labeled **\"M\"** positioned adjacent to the utility line and utility poles.\n*   **Left Boundary (Valley View Road, -E- line):** The large trees labeled **\"SY/M\"** within the shaded street yard buffer are located approximately 10 to 30 feet from the \"-E-\" line and its associated utility pole symbols.\n*   **Top Boundary:** While not explicitly labeled as OHE, there is a line labeled \"-LOC-\" running along the top boundary with trees labeled \"P\", \"M\", and \"P/M\" planted directly adjacent to it.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1447,"outputTokens":799,"totalTokens":4072,"reasoningTokens":1826},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent wil