{"level":30,"time":1776272576296,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines shown on this landscape plan. Where are they located on the site? What trees (if any) are shown nearby? Are conductor lines, poles, or clearance zones marked? Also identify all tree symbols shown and note their locations relative to the OHE lines. Look for any distance dimensions or clearance notes related to trees and overhead electric facilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the findings regarding the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines and associated tree information:\n\n**Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines**\nThe overhead electric lines are located exclusively along the **southern boundary** (bottom edge) of the site plan. They are denoted by a solid line interrupted periodically by the text label **\"-OHE-\"**. This line runs horizontally across almost the entire width of the southern property line, parallel and very close to a wooden privacy fence line (marked with `-x-x-x-` and Key Note H.6).\n\n**Trees Located Nearby the OHE Lines**\nThere is a distinct row of trees shown planted directly along this southern boundary, in close proximity to, or directly underneath, the `-OHE-` line. Moving from left (west) to right (east) along the bottom edge, the trees near the OHE line include:\n*   Two large tree symbols (one dashed, possibly indicating existing; one solid).\n*   Two smaller tree symbols.\n*   A large tree symbol containing the letter **\"M\"** (which Key Notes identify as \"MITIGATION TREE\"), accompanied by the label \"H.7\" (Sod) nearby.\n*   A cluster of three smaller tree symbols, one of which also contains an **\"M\"**.\n*   Another large tree symbol near the southeast corner.\n\n**OHE Markings (Conductors, Poles, Clearance Zones)**\n*   **Conductor Lines:** Individual conductor wires are not drawn. The facility is represented solely by the single center line marked **\"-OHE-\"**.\n*   **Poles:** There are no distinct symbols or labels indicating the specific locations of utility poles supporting the OHE line.\n*   **Clearance Zones:** There are **no clearance zones marked**. Typically, these would appear as dashed offset lines parallel to the OHE line indicating a required \"grow-out\" or safety buffer. None are present on this sheet.\n\n**Identification of All Tree Symbols and Locations**\nThe plan utilizes several types of tree symbols to represent different plantings, primarily differentiated by size and internal line patterns (crosses, branches, etc.). Some are solid (proposed) and some are dashed (existing to remain). Key labels identified within or near tree symbols include **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree), **\"PL\"** (Parking Lot Tree), and occasionally **\"ST\"** (Street Yard Tree).\n*   **Northern Boundary (Top):** A dense, continuous row of large canopy trees is located outside the Limits of Construction (\"-LOC-\") line. Several of these are labeled with **\"M\"** or **\"PL\"**. These are far from the OHE lines.\n*   **Western Boundary (Left):** A cluster of large and small trees is located within a shaded area marked \"H.2\" (Street Yard) along Valley View Road. These are far from the OHE lines.\n*   **Eastern Boundary (Right):** A sparse row of trees runs north-south along the property line, outside the \"-LOC-\" line. These are far from the OHE lines.\n*   **Interior:** Small and medium tree symbols are located within parking lot islands (some labeled **\"PL\"**) and in courtyard areas adjacent to the main building structure. These are far from the OHE lines.\n*   **Southern Boundary (Bottom):** As detailed above, a row of trees is located directly adjacent to the **\"-OHE-\"** line.\n\n**Distance Dimensions or Clearance Notes**\nA thorough review of the plan's linework, dimension lines, and all text sections (\"IRRIGATION NOTES\", \"NOTE\", and \"KEY NOTES\") reveals that **there are no distance dimensions, offset measurements, or specific text notes providing clearance requirements** between the trees and the overhead electric facilities on this specific sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1390,"outputTokens":812,"totalTokens":4932,"reasoningTokens":2730},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines shown on this landscape plan. Where are they located on the site? What trees (if any) are shown nearby? Are conductor lines, poles, or clearance zones marked? Also identify all tree symbols shown and note their locations relative to the OHE lines. Look for any distance dimensions or clearance notes related to trees and overhead electric facilities."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-mX3lEvuAVcS7P2nNcH0yopx9","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Wed, 15 Apr 2026 17:02:56 GMT","server":"Vercel","set-cookie":"_vcrr_9ae7f6aec35bf5b1=dpl_3HJYYwzY7pHyW3BBNhmRbt4tDnvB|0.0713; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=None","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::chgqr-1776272543260-0b375b48d581"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the findings regarding the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines and associated tree information:\n\n**Location of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines**\nThe overhead electric lines are located exclusively along the **southern boundary** (bottom edge) of the site plan. They are denoted by a solid line interrupted periodically by the text label **\"-OHE-\"**. Th