 specifications about transformer pad location, size, or design standards?**\nNo. There are no notes, specifications, or details regarding the physical size, concrete specifications, or design standards for the transformer pads on this sheet.\n*   The **\"Utility Notes\"** block in the bottom right discusses verifying horizontal and vertical locations of existing utilities, point of connection, and specifications for private domestic water and wastewater branches, but mentions nothing about electrical transformers.\n*   The **\"Note\"** block in the bottom left pertains to the \"Yield and Water Flow Mitigation Rule\" and geological inspections, with no mention of electrical infrastructure.\n\n**4) What is the proximity of transformer pads to parking areas, driveways, buildings, and other site features?**\nWhile exact dimensions are not provided (as noted in question 2), visually, the proximity is as follows:\n*   **Pad 1:** Sited immediately adjacent to the primary curved driveway entering the complex, near the western property boundary and \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Pads 2 & 3:** Sited in the perimeter strip between the western facades of the townhome buildings (Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8) and the western property line/easements. They appear to be located in grassy/landscaped areas rather than directly on pavement.\n*   **Pad 4:** Sited in a perimeter strip between the eastern facades of the townhome buildings (Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5) and the eastern property line, adjacent to a \"25' Drainage Easement\".\n*   *Note on parking:* There are no surface parking lots visible in the immediate vicinity of the pads; the buildings appear to be townhomes with internal garages and driveways feeding into the main central access drive.\n\n**5) Are any AE Design approval documents or pad detail references visible on the sheet?**\nNo.\n*   There are no stamps, signatures, or notes indicating Austin Energy (AE) Design approval on this sheet.\n*   There are no detail callouts (e.g., \"See Detail X on Sheet Y\") pointing to the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" symbols to indicate where design specifics can be found. The boxes solely provide the label text."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7087432-bcdb-4375-ad2d-45c773d38896","uuid":"be2fdff5-640b-4800-ac3f-1eeaf5d86e9b","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39) for Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings regarding your specific questions about transformer pads:\n\n**1) The exact location(s) of transformer pads on this site - are they shown and labeled?**\nYes, transformer pads are shown and explicitly labeled on this sheet. There are four distinct locations identified by rectangular symbols with leader lines pointing to text boxes that read exactly: **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n*   **Location 1 (Northwest):** Located near the curved main driveway entrance on the west side of the property, situated west of Bldg. 1.\n*   **Location 2 (West Central):** Located along the western edge of the site, situated between the western exterior wall of Bldg. 2 (near Units 201/202) and the western property line/sidewalk easement.\n*   **Location 3 (Southwest):** Located along the western edge of the site, situated between the western exterior wall of Bldg. 8 (near Units 801/802) and the western property line/sidewalk easement.\n*   **Location 4 (East Central):** Located along the eastern edge of the property, situated in the space to the east of Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 5, near an existing building footprint on the adjacent property.\n\n**2) Are dimensions or clearances shown from the transformer pads to adjacent buildings, parking areas, structures, or other features?**\nNo. There are absolutely no dimension lines, setback measurements, or clearance distances labeled between any of the four \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations and the adjacent buildings, driveways, property lines, or eas