{"level":30,"time":1776272586801,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CNhi6HTQEofnCGVcHfgAiN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016imzTGUwrrYEQCXVrxNHXP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1266,"cache_read_input_tokens":45601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1266},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"6eb0e55a-ad9a-4fda-94e0-37778aa5c973"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272586811,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016imzTGUwrrYEQCXVrxNHXP","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n     2→\n     3→This page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n    11→- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n    12→- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n    13→- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n    14→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n    15→- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n    16→- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n    20→- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n    21→- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"4bf8e3cc-6b3a-4af6-8e08-054ed4435f12","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776272586933,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"This is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for a townhome project. I need to identify and analyze all transformer pads shown on this sheet. Please provide:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations:** Identify the exact location (by building or site area) of each transformer pad shown on the plan\n2. **Transformer Specifications:** What service types are shown (single-phase or three-phase), pad dimensions, and any AE Design detail callouts\n3. **Clearance Evidence:** For each transformer pad, identify:\n   - Clearance distance to buildings/structures\n   - Clearance distance to any fences or site features\n   - Access door orientation\n   - Any access area dimensions (hot-stick use areas)\n   - Positioning relative to utilities, trees, sidewalks, or parking areas\n   - Whether the pad is within any easements\n4. **Underground Utility Routing:** Show how electrical, water, wastewater, and storm drain lines are routed relative to each transformer pad\n5. **Equipment Details:** Are transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type, service phase) shown or referenced? Are bollard details shown?\n6. **Overall Site Layout:** Describe the general positioning of transformers within the site context\n\nPlease be specific about measurements, clearances, and exact locations visible on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the Valley View Townhomes, here is the information regarding the transformer pads as requested.\n\n*Important Note: This is a preliminary layout plan. As such, many specific construction details, dimensions, and specifications typical of a finalized site plan or detailed electrical drawing are absent from this specific sheet.*\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad Locations\nThere are exactly three items explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** on this sheet.\n*   **Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest):** Located in the northwest quadrant of the site. It is situated west of Bldg. 1 (near Unit 101) and north of Bldg. 2 (near Unit 201), adjacent to an internal curved curb/sidewalk.\n*   **Transformer Pad 2 (East-Central):** Located on the eastern side of the site. It is situated between Bldg. 4 (specifically near Unit 404) and Bldg. 5 (specifically near Unit 504), adjacent to an internal straight curb.\n*   **Transformer Pad 3 (Southwest):** Located in the southwest quadrant of the site. It is situated west of Bldg. 8 (specifically near Unit 801) and south of the side of Bldg. 2, adjacent to an internal curved curb/sidewalk.\n\n### 2. Transformer Specifications\n*   **Service Types (Single/Three-phase):** This information is **not provided** on this sheet. There are no notes or labels indicating phase type.\n*   **Pad Dimensions:** There are **no dimensions** given for the transformer pads on this drawing. They are represented by simple square graphics.\n*   **AE Design Detail Callouts:** There are **no callouts** referencing Austin Energy (AE) design criteria, detail numbers, or specific standard specifications on this sheet.\n\n### 3. Clearance Evidence\n*   **Clearance distance to buildings/structures:** The drawing shows physical separation between the square transformer symbols and the building footprints. However, **no explicit dimensions** (e.g., \"10' min clearance\") are provided to quantify this distance.\n*   **Clearance distance to fences or site features:** The pads are drawn near curbs and property boundary lines, but **no clearance dimensions** are labeled.\n*   **Access door orientation:** The drawing consists of plain square boxes. There is **no visual indication** (such as arrows, shading, or \"door\" lines) to show which direction the transformer doors will face.\n*   **Access area dimensions (hot-stick use areas):** There are **no dashed lines or shaded zones** indicating required clear working spaces or hot-stick operation areas around the pads.\n*   **Positioning relative to utilities, trees, sidewalks:**\n    *   All three pads are placed immediately adjacent to internal curbs/sidewalk lines.\n    *   Circular outlines indicating proposed trees are drawn near all three pads.\n    *   The pads are positioned such that underground water (labeled \"-W-\") and wastewater/storm lines route near them, but do not intersect the physical pad footprint shown.\n*   **Easements:** While there are dashed lines indicating easements on the property perimeter (e.g., a \"5' P.U.E.\" on the north edge and a \"Wastewater Easement\" in the northwest), there are **no specific, dimensioned easement boundaries drawn around the transformer pads themselves** to confirm if they sit entirely within dedicated utility easements.\n\n### 4. Underground Utility Routing\nThe primary electrical routing is denoted by solid blue lines marked with \"-E-\".\n*   **Pad 1:** An underground electric line routes from an \"Electrical Pull Box\" near the northwest property line directly to the \"Electrical Transformer Pad.\" From the pad, blue lines branch out to serve \"Electrical Meters\" on Bldgs. 1, 2, and 3. Water (-W-) and Wastewater (-WW-) lines run parallel to the buildings in this area, avoiding the pad.\n*   **Pad 2:** An electric line routes from an \"Electrical Pull Box\" to the pad, then branches out to serve meters on Bldgs. 4, 5, and 6. Water (-W-) and Storm Drain (-SD-) lines run in the adjacent drive aisle, bypassing the pad.\n*   **Pad 3:** An electric line routes down the western perimeter, into an \"Electrical Pull Box,\" and then into the pad. From there, lines branch to serve meters on Bldgs. 7 and 8. A Water (-W-) line runs parallel to the pad area without crossing it.\n\n### 5. Equipment Details\n*   **Transformer Specifications (Oil-filled vs. dry-type, etc.):** This information is **not provided**. The labels only state \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Bollard Details:** There are **no bollards** drawn (typically represented by small circles around the pad), nor are there any text notes calling for protective bollards around any of the transformer pads.\n\n### 6. Overall Site Layout Context\nThe transformers are strategically positioned on the outer perimeter margins of the townhome layout. The site features a central drive aisle loop with buildings inside the loop and around the outer edges. Rather than centralizing power, the design utilizes three distinct transformer hubs pushed to the edges (NW, East, SW) to distribute power locally to clusters of 2 to 3 buildings each. They appear to be placed in landscaped or utility corridor areas between the internal drive curbs and the property boundaries.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1575,"outputTokens":1167,"totalTokens":4656,"reasoningTokens":1914},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for a townhome project. I need to identify and analyze all transformer pads shown on this sheet. Please provide:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations:** Identify the exact location (by building or site area) of each transformer pad shown on the plan\n2. **Transformer Specifications:** What service types are shown (single-phase or three-phase), pad dimensions, and any AE Design detail callouts\n3. **Clearance Evidence:** For each transformer pad, identify:\n   - Clearance distance to buildings/structures\n   - Clearance distance to any fences or site features\n   - Access door orientation\n   - Any access area dimensions (hot-stick use areas)\n   - Positioning relative to utilities, trees, sidewalks, or parking areas\n   - Whether the pad is within any easements\n4. **Underground Utility Routing:** Show how electrical, water, wastewater, and storm drain lines are routed relative to each transformer pad\n5. **Equipment Details:** Are transformer specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type, service phase) shown or referenced? Are bollard details shown?\n6. **Overall Site Layout:** Describe the general positioning of transformers within the site context\n\nPlease be specific about measurements, clearances, and exact locations visible on the plan."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-S7N0hoWwuMZZYhhVz4sM9g1e","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-v