ectrical Meters\" on Bldgs. 1, 2, and 3. Water (-W-) and Wastewater (-WW-) lines run parallel to the buildings in this area, avoiding the pad.\n*   **Pad 2:** An electric line routes from an \"Electrical Pull Box\" to the pad, then branches out to serve meters on Bldgs. 4, 5, and 6. Water (-W-) and Storm Drain (-SD-) lines run in the adjacent drive aisle, bypassing the pad.\n*   **Pad 3:** An electric line routes down the western perimeter, into an \"Electrical Pull Box,\" and then into the pad. From there, lines branch to serve meters on Bldgs. 7 and 8. A Water (-W-) line runs parallel to the pad area without crossing it.\n\n### 5. Equipment Details\n*   **Transformer Specifications (Oil-filled vs. dry-type, etc.):** This information is **not provided**. The labels only state \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Bollard Details:** There are **no bollards** drawn (typically represented by small circles around the pad), nor are there any text notes calling for protective bollards around any of the transformer pads.\n\n### 6. Overall Site Layout Context\nThe transformers are strategically positioned on the outer perimeter margins of the townhome layout. The site features a central drive aisle loop with buildings inside the loop and around the outer edges. Rather than centralizing power, the design utilizes three distinct transformer hubs pushed to the edges (NW, East, SW) to distribute power locally to clusters of 2 to 3 buildings each. They appear to be placed in landscaped or utility corridor areas between the internal drive curbs and the property boundaries."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"210f7c66-b6ac-4c5e-b337-405e381dc733","uuid":"1b0a1b03-07d4-48fe-a01e-35f234b7abf7","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the Valley View Townhomes, here is the information regarding the transformer pads as requested.\n\n*Important Note: This is a preliminary layout plan. As 