{"level":30,"time":1776272614473,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Review the existing conditions survey sheet carefully for any overhead electric utility poles, conductors, or overhead utility lines. Look for:\n1. Any symbols indicating utility poles (typically shown as circles with an X or similar symbol)\n2. Any overhead utility lines (shown as dashed lines with notations like \"O.H.U.L.\" or similar)\n3. Pole locations on the property or immediately adjacent to the property boundaries, especially along Valley View Road or at the property edges\n4. Any indication of electric easements or utility infrastructure\n\nAre there any overhead electric poles or conductors visible on this survey? If so, where are they located relative to the property boundaries?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey sheet, yes, there are overhead electric poles and conductors clearly visible on the property.\n\nHere is a precise description of their locations based on the symbols defined in the document's Legend:\n\n**Symbols Identified per Legend:**\n*   **\"POWER POLE\"**: Indicated by a circle with small lines radiating outward.\n*   **\"O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\"**: Indicated by a line style consisting of a dash followed by two dots (`- .. -`).\n*   **\"GUY ANCHOR\"**: Indicated by a specific symbol attached to power poles.\n\n**Location of Overhead Lines and Poles Relative to Property Boundaries:**\n\nAn overhead utility line network runs along three sides of the property perimeter, generally staying just inside the property boundary lines. Following the continuous path of the lines (starting from near Valley View Road and moving clockwise visually around the page):\n\n1.  **Near Valley View Road (Bottom-Left visually):**\n    *   The overhead line system enters the property near the intersection of **VALLEY VIEW ROAD** and the property boundary labeled `N63°50'57\"W 414.24'`.\n    *   A **\"POWER POLE\"** with a **\"GUY ANCHOR\"** is located just inside the property corner here.\n    *   Text nearby indicates a utility easement: `\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 488, PG. 562 P.R.T.C.TX\"`.\n\n2.  **Along the Bottom Boundary (visually):**\n    *   From the pole near the road, the **\"O.H.U.L.\"** runs the entire length of the property boundary labeled `N63°50'57\"W 414.24'`, parallel to and just inside this line.\n\n3.  **At the Bottom-Right Corner (visually):**\n    *   The line terminates at another **\"POWER POLE\"** located near the corner formed by boundaries `N63°50'57\"W 414.24'` and `S26°15'01\"W 80.67'`. This pole also has an attached **\"GUY ANCHOR\"**.\n    *   Text near this pole indicates another easement: `\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 959, PG. 881 P.R.T.C.TX\"`.\n\n4.  **Along the Right Boundary (visually):**\n    *   From the corner pole, the **\"O.H.U.L.\"** turns and runs upwards, parallel to and just inside the boundary lines labeled `S26°15'01\"W 80.67'` and continuing along `S27°19'28\"W 146.15'`.\n    *   There are two distinct text leaders pointing directly to these line segments, both labeled exactly `\"O.H.U.L.\"`.\n    *   There is a third **\"POWER POLE\"** located roughly midway along this right-side run.\n\n5.  **At the Top-Right Corner (visually):**\n    *   The line reaches a fourth **\"POWER POLE\"** located near the corner formed by boundaries `S27°19'28\"W 146.15'` and `S63°00'28\"E 419.86'`. This pole includes a **\"GUY ANCHOR\"**.\n    *   Text near this pole indicates an easement: `\"10' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 4037, PG. 14 P.R.T.C.TX\"`.\n\n6.  **Along the Top Boundary (visually):**\n    *   From the top-right corner pole, the **\"O.H.U.L.\"** turns left and runs parallel to and just inside the top boundary line labeled `S63°00'28\"E 419.86'`.\n    *   There is a text leader pointing to this line segment labeled exactly `\"O.H.U.L.\"`.\n    *   This overhead line terminates at a fifth **\"POWER POLE\"** located approximately midway along this top boundary line.\n    *   Text near this pole indicates an easement: `\"10' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 5155, PG. 74 P.R.T.C.TX\"`.\n    *   From this fifth pole, an overhead line with a guy anchor extends off the subject property upward into the adjacent lot (\"LOT 4\"). Additionally, an underground electric line drops down from this pole onto the subject property, connecting to a \"TRANSFORMER ON PAD\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1446,"outputTokens":1056,"totalTokens":7005,"reasoningTokens":4503},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Review the existing conditions survey sheet carefully for any overhead electric utility poles, conductors, or overhead utility lines. Look for:\n1. Any symbols indicating utility poles (typically shown as circles with an X or similar symbol)\n2. Any overhead utility lines (shown as dashed lines with notations like \"O.H.U.L.\" or similar)\n3. Pole locations on the property or immediately adjacent to the property boundaries, especially along Valley View Road or at the property edges\n4. Any indication of electric easements or utility infrastructure\n\nAre there any overhead electric poles or conductors visible on this survey? If so, where are they located relative to the property boundaries?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-R6qYd7rgoLqRS2wvN9hY3tfl","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Wed, 15 Apr 2026 17:03:34 GMT","server":"Vercel","set-cookie":"_vcrr_9ae7f6aec35bf5b1=dpl_3HJYYwzY7pHyW3BBNhmRbt4tDnvB|0.0713; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=None","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-verce