{"level":30,"time":1776272645725,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kt9RaXG13eYcbMVbf4QmhD","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n     4→\n     5→[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→\n     8→## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n     9→\n    10→The plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n    11→\n    12→*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n    13→*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n    14→*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n    15→*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n    16→*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n    17→*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n    18→*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n    19→*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n    20→\n    21→## Block 3: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n    22→\n    23→Curb Note:\n    24→Grading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\n    25→away from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n    26→\n    27→## Block 4: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n    28→\n    29→Legend\n    30→[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n    31→[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n    32→[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n    33→700.00\n    34→699.50 Top of Curb\n    35→Bottom of Curb\n    36→[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n    37→[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\n    38→L= Level Landing\n    39→(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\n    40→Down [arrow] ADA Ramp\n    41→(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n    42→\n    43→## Block 5: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n    44→\n    45→Legal Description\n    46→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    47→\n    48→## Block 6: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n    49→\n    50→Benchmarks\n    51→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    52→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    53→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    54→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    55→\n    56→## Block 7: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n    57→\n    58→Tree List\n    59→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    60→\n    61→## Block 11: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n    62→\n    63→Call Before You Dig!!\n    64→\n    65→## Block 12: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n    66→\n    67→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\n    68→applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\n    69→submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    70→\n    71→## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n    72→\n    73→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\n    74→match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\n    75→locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\n    76→construction.\n    77→\n    78→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"0921dd71-c80f-4ef7-9768-e41b4906ed0a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — A graphic scale bar indicating that 1 inch equals 20 feet.\n\n[graphic scale bar with increments 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n\n## Block 2: drawing — This is a detailed grading plan for a multi-family development. It shows existing and proposed contours, building footprints, retaining walls, storm drainage infrastructure, and various utility easements. Key features include multiple buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, each with finished floor elevations (FFE). The plan also indicates existing structures, vegetation, and adjacent property information.\n\nThe plan displays a comprehensive layout for a multi-family development. It includes:\n\n*   **Building Footprints:** Eight buildings labeled Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8, with their respective square footages and finished floor elevations (FFE). For example, Bldg. 1 is 3,290 sf with an FFE of 687.50, and Bldg. 8 is 4,997 sf with an FFE of 685.50.\n*   **Topography:** Existing and proposed contour lines indicating the site's elevation changes.\n*   **Infrastructure:** Proposed storm drain lines, area inlets, and concrete retaining walls.\n*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\n*   **Adjacent Properties:** Information on adjacent properties, such as \"Lot A Cortex Heights Zoning: MF 3-CO Use: Multi-Family\" and \"William Lance Corsbie, Jr. 1.967 Acres Zoning: SF-3 Use: Single Family\".\n*   **Existing Features:** Existing trees, rock rubble, and stone retaining walls.\n*   **Utilities:** Locations of existing water manholes, gas meters, wastewater manholes, and AT&T vaults.\n*   **Specific Details:** The plan includes specific details like a sediment basin, an existing retaining wall to be replaced, and a sidewalk easement.\n\n## Block 3: notes — A note providing specific instructions regarding the construction of grading lines related to curbs.\n\nCurb Note:\nGrading lines that indicate flows toward the curb shall be constructed as a catch curb. Grade lines that indicate flows\naway from curb shall be constructed as a spill curb.\n\n## Block 4: notes — This is the legend for the grading plan, explaining the symbols and line types used to represent various features on the drawing, such as contours, spot elevations, curbs, limits of construction, storm drains, level landings, and ADA ramps.\n\nLegend\n[dashed line] --700-- Existing Contour\n[solid line] --700-- Proposed Contour\n[plus sign] 698.25 Proposed Spot Elevation\n700.00\n699.50 Top of Curb\nBottom of Curb\n[solid line with LOC] Proposed Limits of Construction\n[dashed line with SD] Proposed Storm Drain Line\nL= Level Landing\n(Not to exceed 2% in any Direction)\nDown [arrow] ADA Ramp\n(Not to exceed 8.33%)\n\n## Block 5: notes — Provides the legal description of the property being developed.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 6: notes — Details two benchmark points used for elevation reference on the site plan.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 7: notes — A brief note directing the reader to another sheet for a list of trees.\n\nTree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — A clear instruction to call before starting any excavation work.\n\nCall Before You Dig!!\n\n## Block 12: text_block — A general disclaimer stating that the application does not constitute verification of all data, and the engineer of record is responsible for its completeness and accuracy.\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the\napplicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her\nsubmittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — A note advising that existing utility locations are based on record information and must be field-verified by the contractor prior to construction.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not\nmatch locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility\nlocations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning\nconstruction.\n\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776272645726,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MVEAyug1HXBQafqa8C6Wk1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grading plan blocks.md shows the curb notes and legend but doesn't show transformer locations. Let me use the vision tool to examine both the site plan (Sheet 9) and the grading plan (Sheet 11) together to see transformer pad locations and any drainage patterns. I should also look at the electrical plan more closely with another vision call focused on specific clearances and utilities.\n\nLet me call the vision tool on the electrical plan again but with more specific questions about utilities, particularly looking for:\n- Proximity to water/wastewater/storm drain lines\n- Whether transformers are in parking areas\n- Whether bollards are visible\n- Clearances to buildings","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":58528,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"7264883e-0f63-492e-a10a-19bd40aff3ae"}
