{"level":30,"time":1776272645728,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and describe:\n1. Are the existing utility poles and overhead utility lines shown from the existing conditions survey visible on this proposed site plan?\n2. Where are they located relative to the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8)?\n3. Are there any dimension annotations or clearance notes showing horizontal or vertical clearances from the overhead lines to buildings, driveways, or other site features?\n4. Do the buildings, parking areas, driveways, or retaining walls appear to be positioned with adequate clearance from the overhead lines?\n5. Are there any notations about utility coordination, pole relocation, or clearance verification?\n\nThe site plan shows Buildings 1-8, driveways, parking, the detention pond, and retaining walls. Please assess how the proposed layout relates to the existing overhead facilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan (Sheet 9), here are the findings regarding the existing utility poles and overhead lines:\n\n**1. Are the existing utility poles and overhead utility lines shown from the existing conditions survey visible on this proposed site plan?**\nYes, overhead utility lines and poles are visible on this site plan.\n*   There is a distinct line type labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** (indicating Overhead Electric) running horizontally across the lower (southern) portion of the site plan.\n*   Along this \"- OHE -\" line, there are multiple circular symbols with crosshairs inside them, which are standard representations for utility poles.\n*   Additionally, in the upper left corner near the wastewater service connection, there is a specific label pointing to an **\"AT&T Pole\"**.\n\n**2. Where are they located relative to the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8)?**\n*   **Southern OHE Line:** The primary overhead electric line runs east-to-west along the southern edge of the property boundary. It is located entirely south of the proposed southern driving aisle/fire lane and parking spaces. **Building 7** and **Building 8** are the closest structures to this line, but they are positioned north of the driving aisle, creating a substantial horizontal separation between the buildings and the overhead line.\n*   **Top Left Pole:** The \"AT&T Pole\" is located at the far northwest edge of the site plan, outside the main property boundary, near the existing roadway and the proposed northern \"Construct Type II Driveway\". It is far to the west of Building 1.\n\n**3. Are there any dimension annotations or clearance notes showing horizontal or vertical clearances from the overhead lines to buildings, driveways, or other site features?**\nNo. While there are numerous dimension lines indicating building footprints (e.g., \"46.9'\", \"21.3'\"), driveway widths (\"26.0'\"), and property boundaries, there are **no dimension lines or specific text annotations indicating horizontal or vertical clearance distances** from the \"- OHE -\" lines or poles to any proposed building, retaining wall, or driveway edge.\n\n**4. Do the buildings, parking areas, driveways, or retaining walls appear to be positioned with adequate clearance from the overhead lines?**\nBased strictly on the 2D layout presented on this sheet:\n*   The overhead lines do not cross over the footprint of any proposed building (Buildings 1-8).\n*   The \"- OHE -\" line appears to run parallel to, and mostly south of, the proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" located along the southern edge of the driveway.\n*   Visually, there is a distinct horizontal separation on the plan between the overhead lines/poles and the paved areas/buildings.\n*   *Note:* Because there are no vertical elevation details for the lines or horizontal clearance dimension lines provided on this specific sheet, absolute confirmation of \"adequate\" regulatory or safety clearance cannot be determined solely from this image.\n\n**5. Are there any notations about utility coordination, pole relocation, or clearance verification?**\nNo. A review of the provided text blocks on this sheet yields no specific notations regarding utility coordination, pole relocation, or clearance verification.\n*   The **\"Site Plan Release Notes\"** discuss compliance with chapters, demolition, certificates of occupancy, and ROW excavation, but do not mention overhead utilities.\n*   The **\"General Notes\"** (such as Accessibility, Lighting, Trash Collection) do not address overhead lines.\n*   There is a standard **\"Texas 811 Call Before You Dig!!\"** warning box regarding underground utilities, but no specific directive regarding the overhead lines.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1481,"outputTokens":773,"totalTokens":3950,"reasoningTokens":1696},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and describe:\n1. Are the existing utility poles and overhead utility lines shown from the existing conditions survey visible on this proposed site plan?\n2. Where are they located relative to the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8)?\n3. Are there any dimension annotations or clearance notes showing horizontal or vertical clearances from the overhead lines to buildings, driveways, or other site features?\n4. Do the buildings, parking areas, driveways, or retaining walls appear to be positioned with adequate clearance from the overhead lines?\n5. Are there any notations about utility coordination, pole relocation, or clearance verification?\n\nThe site plan shows Buildings 1-8, driveways, parking, the detention pond, and retaining walls. Please assess how the proposed layout relates to the existing overhead facilities."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-5IAIqusuuLDJklGNIwYbqJs6","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","cont