{"level":30,"time":1776272645729,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify: 1) Are transformer pads marked or labeled on this site plan? 2) If so, what are their locations relative to buildings, parking, driveways, and property lines? 3) Are any dimensions or clearances shown from transformer pads to these features? 4) Are any notes about utilities, electrical service, or transformer placement visible? 5) What buildings, structures, or site features are closest to where the transformer pads would be located?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Are transformer pads marked or labeled on this site plan?**\nYes, a transformer pad is explicitly labeled on the site plan. There is a leader line with text pointing to a small rectangular feature that reads exactly: \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\".\n\n**2) If so, what are their locations relative to buildings, parking, driveways, and property lines?**\n*   **Relative to Property Lines:** The labeled transformer pad is located on the far western (left) edge of the site, situated very close to the western property line boundary.\n*   **Relative to Driveways:** It is located immediately west of the main entrance driveway, labeled \"**Construct Type II Driveway**\".\n*   **Relative to Buildings:** It is located directly west of **Bldg. 8** and southwest of **Bldg. 1**.\n*   **Relative to Parking:** It is separated from the main internal parking areas by the entrance driveway and the buildings. There is no parking immediately adjacent to it.\n\n**3) Are any dimensions or clearances shown from transformer pads to these features?**\nNo explicit dimensions (such as width and length of the pad) or clearance zones (such as a dashed working clearance radius) are shown originating from or pointing directly to the transformer pad itself. There is a dimension of \"**26.6'**\" spanning from the western property line to the western edge of the main driveway in the general vicinity of the pad, but it does not specifically dimension the pad or its clearances.\n\n**4) Are any notes about utilities, electrical service, or transformer placement visible?**\n*   **Transformers:** The only specific note regarding transformer placement is the \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" label itself.\n*   **Electrical/Utility Easements:** On the opposite (eastern/right) side of the property, there are notes for electrical easements, including:\n    *   \"**5' Electric Easement**\"\n    *   \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement**\"\n*   **General Utilities:** The \"Site Plan Release Notes\" table (item 'e') mentions: \"*Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin...*\" but does not explicitly mention electrical service providers or transformer standards.\n*   Other specific utility points are labeled near the main entrance (northwest corner), such as \"**Wastewater Service Connection**\", \"**Water Meter**\", and \"**AT&T Ped**\".\n\n**5) What buildings, structures, or site features are closest to where the transformer pads would be located?**\nThe features closest to the labeled transformer pad are:\n*   The main entrance driveway (\"**Construct Type II Driveway**\") immediately to the east.\n*   The western property line immediately to the west.\n*   A feature immediately adjacent labeled \"**Tree Well (need to look up approap. detail)**\".\n*   A \"**Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk**\" that runs parallel to the driveway nearby.\n*   **Bldg. 8** is the closest building structure, located to the east across the driveway.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1411,"outputTokens":678,"totalTokens":4131,"reasoningTokens