{"level":30,"time":1776272645730,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Please examine this existing conditions survey sheet and identify all overhead utility infrastructure. Specifically:\n\n1. Are there overhead utility poles shown on the property or adjacent to it? If yes, describe their locations.\n2. Are there overhead utility lines (conductors) shown? If yes, which direction do they run?\n3. Are there any overhead electric transformer pads shown?\n4. Are there any down guy wires or guy anchors shown?\n5. What buildings, structures, driveways, or other site features are near these overhead lines?\n\nPlease be specific about locations (north side, south side, east, west, along property line, etc.) and describe what's shown clearly.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey sheet, here is the information regarding the overhead utility infrastructure:\n\n**1. Are there overhead utility poles shown on the property or adjacent to it?**\nYes, there are utility poles shown adjacent to the property. They are located along the western boundary of the site, running parallel to Valley View Road. Based on the symbols (solid black circles), there are at least three poles depicted along this frontage: one near the northwest corner, one roughly midway along the western property line, and one near the southwest corner.\n\n**2. Are there overhead utility lines (conductors) shown? If yes, which direction do they run?**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown.\n*   A primary line runs generally **North-South** along the western property line, following the path of Valley View Road, connecting the utility poles mentioned above.\n*   Additionally, there is a service drop line that runs roughly **West-to-East**. It originates from the middle utility pole on Valley View Road and crosses the property to connect to the primary existing building.\n\n**3. Are there any overhead electric transformer pads shown?**\n*(Note: \"Overhead transformer pads\" mixes terminology; transformers are typically either pole-mounted overhead or pad-mounted on the ground).*\nA visual scan of the drawing does not reveal any clearly labeled pole-mounted transformers on the identified utility poles, nor are there any clearly discernible or explicitly labeled pad-mounted electrical transformers shown on the ground near these lines.\n\n**4. Are there any down guy wires or guy anchors shown?**\nYes, guy wires and anchors are depicted. They are shown extending outward from the utility poles located near the outer edges of the property's road frontage (specifically, anchored from the pole near the northwest corner and the pole near the southwest corner), pointing away from the main parcel.\n\n**5. What buildings, structures, driveways, or other site features are near these overhead lines?**\n*   **Near the North-South main lines:** These lines run directly adjacent to Valley View Road, concrete driveways (\"CONC. DRIVE\"), concrete walkways, various fences (including \"WOOD FENCE\"), and numerous trees situated along the western property boundary.\n*   **Near the West-to-East service drop line:** This line crosses over the front yard area of the property. It passes near/over a concrete walkway (\"CONC.\"), various trees/vegetation, and terminates directly at the primary existing building structure centrally located on the lot (labeled with \"SLAB F.F.E = 686.8'\").","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1452,"outputTokens":541,"totalTokens":5539,"reasoningTokens":3546},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subs