{"level":30,"time":1776272645730,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"This is the main Site Plan for Valley View Townhomes. I need to identify transformer pads and assess clearances. Please provide:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations on This Sheet:** Are transformer pads shown or labeled? If yes, describe their exact locations relative to building numbers\n2. **Visible Clearances:** What is shown about clearance distances to:\n   - Buildings/structures\n   - Parking areas or drive aisles\n   - Sidewalks or walkways\n   - Any utility easements or infrastructure\n3. **Site Context Around Each Transformer:** Are there trees, dumpsters, hydrants, bollards, or other site elements shown near the transformer locations?\n4. **Dimension Analysis:** Are any clearance dimensions, pad dimensions, or spacing measurements labeled on or near transformer locations?\n5. **Property Boundaries and Easements:** Are transformer pads shown in relation to the property lines or any dedicated easements?\n\nBe as specific as possible about what is or is not visible on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close visual analysis of the provided site plan for Valley View Townhomes, here is the information regarding transformer pads and their clearances:\n\n**1. Transformer Pad Locations on This Sheet**\n*   **Labeled Location:** There is one explicitly labeled transformer pad on this sheet. On the middle-left side of the plan, there is a text box that reads precisely **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"**. \n*   **Exact Placement:** The leader line from this label points to a small rectangular box located to the west of **\"Bldg. 2\"** (specifically adjacent to the front area of **\"Unit 201\"**). It sits between the building and the main northern entry driveway.\n*   **Other Locations:** Although the label includes \"(Typ.)\" (indicating typical), there are no other clearly marked or identically labeled transformer pads visible adjacent to the other buildings (Bldg. 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, or 8) on this specific sheet.\n\n**2. Visible Clearances**\nNo specific clearance radii, arcs, or dimensions are graphically drawn around the transformer pad. Based purely on the scaled drawing lines:\n*   **To Buildings/Structures:** The pad is separated from \"Bldg. 2\" by a walkway. No numerical distance is provided.\n*   **To Parking/Drive aisles:** The pad is located just east of the main entrance drive (labeled **\"Construct Type III Driveway\"**). It appears to sit just outside the driveway curb line, separated by a sidewalk.\n*   **To Sidewalks or Walkways:** The pad appears to be immediately adjacent to (abutting) the sidewalk that runs parallel to the driveway, and a walkway leading to Unit 201. \n*   **To Utility easements/infrastructure:** The pad is located near a **\"Sidewalk Easement\"**. There are utility lines running nearby (a water line marked with \"W\" and a line marked with \"E\" along the main road), but no specific clearance distances to these lines are labeled.\n\n**3. Site Context Around Each Transformer**\n*   **Trees/Landscaping:** Immediately south of the labeled transformer pad, there is a square feature labeled **\"Tree Well\"** with a leader pointing directly next to the transformer location. \n*   **Other Elements:** There are no dumpsters, fire hydrants, or bollards shown or labeled in the immediate vicinity of this transformer pad. (Note: Bollards are labeled elsewhere on the site, such as **\"Bollard (Typ)\"** near Bldg. 4, but not near this transformer).\n\n**4. Dimension Analysis**\n*   **Pad Dimensions:** There are no length or width dimensions labeled on the transformer pad itself.\n*   **Clearance/Spacing Measurements:** There are no clearance dimensions (e.g., \"10' min clearance\") labeled near or around the transformer location. There is a **\"3'\"** dimension labeled on the walkway path right next to the pad/tree well area, but this denotes the width of the pedestrian path, not a transformer clearance.\n\n**5. Property Boundaries and Easements**\n*   The transformer pad is located well within the site's western property line. \n*   It is situated just east of a labeled **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** area that runs along the main roadway frontage. \n*   Note: There is a **\"3' Electric Easement\"** labeled on the far right (eastern) side of the property, but no transformer pads are drawn or labeled within that specific easement on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1511,"outputTokens":762,"totalTokens":4964,"reasoningTokens":2691},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look 