 are depicted. They are shown extending outward from the utility poles located near the outer edges of the property's road frontage (specifically, anchored from the pole near the northwest corner and the pole near the southwest corner), pointing away from the main parcel.\n\n**5. What buildings, structures, driveways, or other site features are near these overhead lines?**\n*   **Near the North-South main lines:** These lines run directly adjacent to Valley View Road, concrete driveways (\"CONC. DRIVE\"), concrete walkways, various fences (including \"WOOD FENCE\"), and numerous trees situated along the western property boundary.\n*   **Near the West-to-East service drop line:** This line crosses over the front yard area of the property. It passes near/over a concrete walkway (\"CONC.\"), various trees/vegetation, and terminates directly at the primary existing building structure centrally located on the lot (labeled with \"SLAB F.F.E = 686.8'\")."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6450ffe4-612c-4eea-8b35-57aec9f3f591","uuid":"de604927-953f-4d00-887f-62915706fdec","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey sheet, here is the information regarding the overhead utility infrastructure:\n\n**1. Are there overhead utility poles shown on the property or adjacent to it?**\nYes, there are utility poles shown adjacent to the property. They are located along the western boundary of the site, running parallel to Valley View Road. Based on the symbols (solid black circles), there are at least three poles depicted along this frontage: one near the northwest corner, one roughly midway along the western property line, and one near the southwest corner.\n\n**2. Are there overhead utility lines (conductors) shown? If yes, which direction do they run?**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown.\n*   A primary line runs generally **North-South** along the western property line, following the path of Valley V