truction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n    28→*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n    29→*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n    30→*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n    31→*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n    32→*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n    33→*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n    34→\n    35→---\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"210f7c66-b6ac-4c5e-b337-405e381dc733","uuid":"f94fc7d8-3cc8-409b-b465-ee1ce732d843","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Grading Plan\n\nThis sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
