"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":504946.955308,"endTime":571435.634606,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"5MTfaaHRJ9ftle0PpcbsqAw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.108696","marketCost":"0.108696","inferenceCost":"0.108696","inputInferenceCost":"0.002796","outputInferenceCost":"0.1059","generationId":"gen_01KP91J6QVSGA5NMAJGYMRPASE"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272679623,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8oEjVJrLsQXXn5jr3vVEd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided proposed site plan (Sheet 9), here are the findings regarding the overhead utilities and clearances:\n\n**1. Overhead utility poles and lines:**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown on the proposed site plan. A line clearly labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric) runs along the entire southern (bottom) property line. Several utility poles and guy wires are also depicted along this line (e.g., near the callouts for \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\"). There is also an \"AT&T Post\" and a pole shown near the northwestern (top-left) entrance. \n\n**2. Proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8):**\n**Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are the closest proposed buildings to the overhead utility lines. They are located in the southern half of the site, situated just north of the southern driveway loop that separates them from the \"- OHE -\" line running along the bottom property boundary. Buildings 1-6 are situated further north and east, further away from this specific line.\n\n**3. Proposed driveways and parking areas:**\nThe southern section of the main driveway loop and its adjacent perpendicular parking spaces run parallel to, and very closely to, the southern property line and the \"- OHE -\" line. While the \"- OHE -\" line appears to roughly trace the property boundary just outside the retaining wall, the close proximity of the driveway and parking areas to these lines means they are within the immediate vicinity and would likely require vertical clearance verification (16-18 feet) to account for line sag over the right-of-way or easements. \n\n**4. Clearance dimensions:**\n**No.** There are absolutely no dimension annotations indicating either horizontal or vertical clearances from the overhead poles or conductors to the proposed buildings, driveways, parking spaces, or retaining walls. The drawing includes standard site layout dimensions (like the 24' drive aisle width or building footprint dimensions), but nothing specifically targeting utility clearances.\n\n**5. Landscape/tree locations:**\nYes, there are tree symbols depicted near the overhead lines. Specifically, there are tree symbols located near the bottom-left property boundary (near the \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" note) and near the bottom-right property corner (near the \"5' Elec. Easement\" note), placing them in close proximity to the \"- OHE -\" line.\n\n### Conclusion:\n**Deficiency identified.** While the overhead utilities (\"- OHE -\") and poles are clearly shown on the proposed site plan along the southern boundary, the required **clearance dimensions** (vertical or horizontal) verifying safe distances between these utilities and the proposed structures, driveways, or landscaping are completely missing from this sheet."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b9758a-7404-4795-a19d-c8c5d3a54014","uuid":"26ed2530-38e6-4a8a-870b-7eb4652114c0","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided proposed site plan (Sheet 9), here are the findings regarding the overhead utilities and clearances:\n\n**1. Overhead utility poles and lines:**\nYes, overhead utility lines are shown on the proposed site plan. A line clearly labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric) runs along the entire southern (bottom) property line. Several utility poles and guy wires are also depicted along this line (e.g., near the callouts for \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\"). There is also an \"AT&T Post\" and a pole shown near the northwestern (top-left) entrance. \n\n**2. Proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8):**\n**Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are the closest proposed buildings to the overhead utility lines. They are located in the southern half of the site, situated just north of the southern driveway loop that separates them from the \"- OHE -\" line running along the bottom property boundary. Buildings 1-6 are situated further north and east, further away from this specific line.\n\n**3. Proposed driveways and parking areas:**\nThe southern section of the main driveway loop and its adjacent perpendicular parking spaces run parallel to, and very closely to, the southern property line and the \"- OHE -\" line. While the \"- OHE -\" line appears to roughly trace the property boundary just outside the retaining wall, the close proximity of the driveway and parking areas to these lines means they are within the immediate vicinity and would likely require vertical clearance verification (16-18 feet) to account for line sag over the right-of-way or easements. \n\n**4. Clearance dimensions:**\n**No.** There are absolutely no dimension annotations indicating either horizontal or vertical clearances from the overhead poles or conductors to the proposed buildings, driveways, parking spaces, or retaining walls. The drawing includes standard site layout dimensions (like the 24' drive aisle width or building footprint dimensions), but nothing specifically targeting utility clearances.\n\n**5. Landscape/tree locations:**\nYes, there are tree symbols depicted near the overhead lines. Specifically, there are tree symbols located near the bottom-left property boundary (near the \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" note) and near the bottom-right property corner (near the \"5' Elec. Easement\" note), placing them in close proximity to the \"- OHE -\" line.\n\n### Conclusion:\n**Deficiency identified.** While the overhead utilities (\"- OHE -\") and poles are clearly shown on the proposed site plan along the southern boundary, the required **clearance dimensions** (vertical or horizontal) verifying safe distances between