{"level":30,"time":1776272709463,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01B4kdPBNsWgwhbqLAeovk8t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HHmZBg4SL6apDUZ34Tgp9","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan carefully to identify:\n\n1. **Overhead utility infrastructure**: Locate and note any overhead electric lines (labeled O.H.E., O.H.U.L., or similar) or utility poles shown on the plan.\n\n2. **Tree locations near overhead utilities**: Identify all trees (marked with symbols like \"+\", circles, or letters like \"SY\", \"PL\", \"P\", \"M\") that are located near the overhead electric lines. Note their approximate distances from the lines and poles.\n\n3. **Tree species identification**: Are tree species labels provided? Can you identify which specific trees are proposed near the overhead utilities?\n\n4. **Clearance dimensions**: Are there any dimension annotations or notes showing clearances between proposed trees and overhead conductors?\n\n5. **Utility-compatible tree markers**: Does the plan indicate which trees (if any) are utility-compatible (typically marked with \"UC\" designation per ECM Appendix F)?\n\n6. **Electric easement areas**: Are the electric easements shown, and do they contain any tree plantings?\n\nWhat trees are proposed within 10-50 feet of the overhead electric utilities, and are they verified as utility-compatible species?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1645,"cache_read_input_tokens":53744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1645},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b9758a-7404-4795-a19d-c8c5d3a54014","uuid":"48c00ef0-c7c8-4c94-ad37-b42c78c9d325"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272709463,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan carefully to identify:\n\n1. **Overhead utility infrastructure**: Locate and note any overhead electric lines (labeled O.H.E., O.H.U.L., or similar) or utility poles shown on the plan.\n\n2. **Tree locations near overhead utilities**: Identify all trees (marked with symbols like \"+\", circles, or letters like \"SY\", \"PL\", \"P\", \"M\") that are located near the overhead electric lines. Note their approximate distances from the lines and poles.\n\n3. **Tree species identification**: Are tree species labels provided? Can you identify which specific trees are proposed near the overhead utilities?\n\n4. **Clearance dimensions**: Are there any dimension annotations or notes showing clearances between proposed trees and overhead conductors?\n\n5. **Utility-compatible tree markers**: Does the plan indicate which trees (if any) are utility-compatible (typically marked with \"UC\" designation per ECM Appendix F)?\n\n6. **Electric easement areas**: Are the electric easements shown, and do they contain any tree plantings?\n\nWhat trees are proposed within 10-50 feet of the overhead electric utilities, and are they verified as utility-compatible species?","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272709464,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KrJDin5cLUAbBzXSzMdLG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is EXTREMELY important information! I found the critical notes about tree placement and transmission lines. Let me highlight the key points:\n\n**Electric Notes (Distribution):**\n1. Austin Energy has the right to prune/remove trees and obstructions in easements\n2. Owner must provide easement access\n3. **Owner is responsible for tree pruning within 10 feet of proposed overhead electric facilities**\n4. Owner must maintain clearances per NESC and OSHA\n5. Relocation costs are owner's responsibility\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes:**\n1. **\"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\"** - This is explicit and categorical\n2. No digging/grading within 25 feet of transmission structures\n3. Pre-construction meeting required with Austin Energy\n4. Barricades 10 feet from transmission structures\n5. 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction (OSHA)\n6-16. Various other construction and maintenance requirements\n\nNow the critical question is: **Is there a transmission easement on this property?**\n\nFrom the facts.md file, I saw:\n- Plat-dedicated \"5' Electric Easements (×2)\" - these are distribution, not transmission\n- No transmission easement mentioned in the recorded easements\n\nSo it appears this site has **distribution electric service** (through the 5' electric easements), **NOT transmission**. The transmission notes on Sheet 3 appear to be general template language that may apply if transmission exists, but the specific electric transmission easements are not mentioned as being on this property.\n\nHowever, the vision analysis of Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) clearly showed:\n- A line marked \"-OHE-\" (overhead electric) on the southern boundary\n- Trees planted directly along this OHE line\n- No clearance zones or dimensions shown\n- No Austin Energy approval documentation visible on the landscape plan\n\n\nThe service type matters significantly—distribution systems require 15 feet clearance for standard trees and 25 feet for large species, while transmission systems prohibit any trees within 25 feet of structures entirely. I need to verify whether this property has distribution or transmission service, measure the actual distances from the planted trees to the overhead electric line, identify the tree species near the OHE line, and determine if any are utility-compatible species.\n\nI'll use the distance measurement tool on Sheet 31 to check how far the trees are positioned from the OHE line.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":53942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d155abec-404b-4144-83fe-2ada3fa35846","uuid":"22efecb5-5902-450b-a217-9fdf0f6da273"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272709464,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KrJDin5cLUAbBzXSzMdLG9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! I found critical notes about tree placement near electric facilities. The notes show that:\n\n1. For **distribution lines**: Owner is responsible for tree pruning within 10 feet of overhead electric facilities\n2. For **transmission lines** (if applicable): \"No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure.\"\n\nNow let me measure the distances from the trees shown near the overhead electric line on Sheet 31 to understand if they comply with the clearance requirements. First, let me use the vision tool again to identify specific tree locations that need measurement:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":53942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d155abec-404b-4144-83fe-2ada3fa35846","uuid":"639b2f98-2e2b-4f3a-aa9a-5cbc23eb0319"}
