{"level":30,"time":1776272709464,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Look at the southern boundary of the site plan where the overhead electric (OHE) line is located. Identify and describe each tree or tree cluster within approximately 25-30 feet of the OHE line. For each tree or group, describe: (1) its approximate location on the southern boundary (e.g., \"far left/southwest corner,\" \"center-south,\" etc.); (2) the symbols or labels within or near the tree symbol (e.g., \"M\" for mitigation, \"PL\" for parking lot); (3) any text labels or plant type indicators associated with it. This will help identify which specific trees need distance verification.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272709464,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LebcwC8J7QbywiB4hHnK1U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my research, let me now systematically evaluate each checklist item. I've confirmed that:\n\n1. **Overhead electric lines ARE depicted on the landscape plan** - labeled \"-OHE-\" along the southern boundary and \"-E-\" along the western boundary (Valley View Road)\n2. **Trees are proposed very close to these lines** - trees in the southern landscape buffer and western street yard buffer are within 10-30 feet of the overhead electric lines\n3. **No clearance dimensions or Austin Energy approval are documented** on the plans\n4. **The proposed tree species are**: Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud\n\nNow let me compile my findings for each of the 15 checklist items:\n\n## **Research Summary - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n\n- **No clearance measurements** shown from any proposed trees to overhead electric conductors or poles\n- **No documentation of utility-compatible (UC) status** from ECM Appendix F for any proposed tree species on the landscape plans\n- **No documentation of mature heights** from ECM Appendix F for proposed tree species  \n- **No Austin Energy written approval** for trees planted near overhead electric lines\n- **No visual differentiation** of \"large trees\" (40+ feet) on the landscape plan\n- **No root barrier details** shown for any trees potentially near underground electric equipment\n- **Trees clearly shown within restricted zones** but without notation of compliance or special provisions\n\n## **Evaluation of Each Checklist Item:**\n\n**EL-2.1 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 lateral feet of distribution conductor:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- While trees are shown on the landscape plan, the plan does not identify the utility-compatible status (UC designation from ECM Appendix F) for any species\n- Cannot verify whether non-UC trees are within 15 feet of distribution conductors without documented species identification and clearance measurements\n\n**EL-2.2 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductor:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**  \n- No transmission facilities are identified on the site plan; all overhead lines appear to be distribution class (-E- and -OHE- labels suggest distribution)\n- Cannot assess this item without confirmation that transmission facilities exist\n\n**EL-2.3 - Large trees (40+ feet) within 25 lateral feet of distribution conductor:**\n- **Status: FAIL**\n- The landscape plan shows trees (including Cedar Elm and Live Oak plantings) within 25 feet of the overhead electric lines depicted on the plan\n- Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) typically has a mature height of 50-70 feet, qualifying as a \"large tree\" per ECM Appendix F thresholds\n- Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) typically has a mature height of 40-50+ feet, also a \"large tree\"\n- These large trees are shown on the landscape plan in close proximity to the -OHE- and -E- utility lines\n- No documentation of clearance measurements or variances provided\n\n**EL-2.4 - Large trees (40+ feet) within 50 lateral feet of transmission conductor:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- No transmission facilities are confirmed on the site; no assessment possible\n\n**EL-2.5 - Trees within transmission easement boundaries:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- No transmission easement is identified on the site plan; not applicable or cannot be verified\n\n**EL-2.6 - Trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility pole:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**  \n- The landscape plan shows utility poles on both boundaries, but specific distances from tree trunk centers to pole locations are not dimensioned\n- The vision analysis indicated trees \"approximately 10 to 30 feet\" from utility poles on the western boundary, suggesting some trees may be within 10 feet, but cannot be verified without precise clearance dimensions on the plan\n\n**EL-2.7 - Trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted electric equipment or between access door and drivable surface:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) shows underground transformer pads and pull boxes within the property\n- The landscape plan does not show the relationship between proposed trees and these pad-mounted equipment locations relative to each other\n- Cannot verify clearances without overlay or dimensioning between landscape plan and electrical plan\n\n**EL-2.8 - Trees within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- Sheet 21 shows underground electric equipment and transformer pads, but the landscape plan does not dimension tree locations relative to this underground infrastructure\n- Cannot verify compliance without documentation of distances\n\n**EL-2.9 - Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment lack root barriers:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- The landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not identify which trees are within 20 feet of underground electric equipment from Sheet 21\n- No root barrier specifications are shown on the landscape details (Sheet 37)\n- Cannot verify compliance\n\n**EL-2.10 - Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities:**\n- **Status: FAIL**\n- While Sheet 35 (Plant Schedule) identifies tree species by common and scientific name, these species identifications are NOT cross-referenced on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) itself\n- The landscape plan shows tree symbols (circles, labeled SY, PL, M, P) but does not identify which specific species correspond to which locations\n- The plan does not indicate which trees (e.g., \"Cedar Elm\" vs. \"Live Oak\" vs. \"Texas Mountain Laurel\") are being planted near the overhead electric lines\n- Trees must be identifiable on the landscape plan itself relative to electric facilities, not just in a separate schedule\n\n**EL-2.11 - Large trees not differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities:**\n- **Status: FAIL**\n- The landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not differentiate \"large trees\" (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from small trees\n- There is no legend indicating mature height categories or large tree designation\n- All trees near overhead electric infrastructure are shown with the same symbol types (SY, PL, M)\n- Cannot verify clearance compliance when large trees and non-large trees are indistinguishable on the plan\n\n**EL-2.12 - Tree clearances measured from utility pole centerline or structure instead of from outer conductor:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan between trees and electric infrastructure\n- Cannot assess measurement methodology when no measurements are documented\n\n**EL-2.13 - Tree clearances measured from tree canopy instead of from tree trunk:**\n- **Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan\n- Cannot assess measurement methodology\n\n**EL-2.14 - Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities, preventing clearance verification:**\n- **Status: FAIL**\n- While trees are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) AND overhead electric facilities are shown on the landscape plan, the two are NOT clearly related\n- There are no dimension lines, callouts, or notes showing how trees relate to overhead electric conductors and poles\n- The landscape plan shows \"OHE\" and \"E\" utility lines, but does not provide clearance information or notes indicating compliance\n- A reviewer cannot verify clearances from the landscape plan as presented\n\n**EL-2.15 - Trees proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval:**\n- **Status: FAIL**\n- Trees are shown on the landscape plan clearly in proximity to overhead electric lines (<30 feet based on visual analysis)\n- No written approval from Austin Energy authorizing trees in restricted zones is visible on the submitted plans\n- No notes or references indicating that special approval has been obtained\n- The grouping specifically states that \"Plans proposing trees within prohibited zones must include documented Austin Energy approval or the violation must be flagged\"\n\nNow let me compile the findings in the required format:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2236,"cache_read_input_tokens":58315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2236},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3857099-05e9-4b26-b534-a07960b24bfd","uuid":"ba753e7f-0309-4674-b9af-f481d778eb04"}
