{"level":30,"time":1776272709467,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine the landscape plan and address the following questions about overhead electric lines and proposed site features:\n\n1. Are overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on this landscape plan? If yes, describe their routing.\n2. What is the location and routing of the proposed driveways, parking areas, sidewalks, and buildings relative to the overhead electric lines?\n3. Are there any trees or landscaping proposed near or beneath the overhead electric lines? If yes, what species are proposed?\n4. What is the distance between proposed buildings and the overhead electric lines?\n5. Are there any clearance dimensions or notes shown regarding overhead electric lines?\n\nPlease be specific about locations and features visible on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the answers to your questions regarding overhead electric lines and proposed site features:\n\n1.  **Are overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on this landscape plan? If yes, describe their routing.**\n    Yes, overhead electric lines are shown. They are indicated by a line style labeled **\"-OHE-\"** routing horizontally across the very bottom (southern) edge of the site plan, appearing to run parallel to or slightly outside the bottom property line/limit of construction.\n\n2.  **What is the location and routing of the proposed driveways, parking areas, sidewalks, and buildings relative to the overhead electric lines?**\n    *   **Buildings:** The proposed buildings are centrally located on the site and are set back significantly to the north (above) the OHE line running along the southern boundary.\n    *   **Driveways and Parking Areas:** The primary driveway and parking area (shaded grey and keyed as \"H.1 PROPOSED PAVING\") is located on the left (western) side of the site. It runs perpendicular to the OHE line, terminating near the bottom left corner but remaining north of the OHE routing.\n    *   **Sidewalks:** Sidewalks are primarily shown wrapping around the buildings and along the western edge near the parking. They are located well north of the OHE line at the bottom of the plan.\n\n3.  **Are there any trees or landscaping proposed near or beneath the overhead electric lines? If yes, what species are proposed?**\n    Yes, there are several proposed trees plotted along the southern boundary line in close proximity to the \"-OHE-\" line.\n    *   **Species:** Specific botanical species (e.g., Oak, Elm) are **not** listed on this sheet. The trees in this area are labeled with generic tags such as **\"M\"** or **\"H.7\"**. According to the legend below the KEY NOTES, **\"M\"** stands for **\"MITIGATION TREE\"** and **\"H.7\"** in the Key Notes refers to **\"SOD\"**.\n\n4.  **What is the distance between proposed buildings and the overhead electric lines?**\n    There is no explicit dimension line or text on this sheet specifying the exact distance between the proposed buildings and the OHE line. Visually, based on the provided graphic scale (1\" = 20'-0\"), there appears to be a substantial setback (roughly estimated at 30-40+ feet, though not explicitly verified by a labeled dimension) between the southernmost building facade and the OHE line.\n\n5.  **Are there any clearance dimensions or notes shown regarding overhead electric lines?**\n    No. I have reviewed the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", the general \"NOTE\" section, the \"KEY NOTES\", and the linework on the plan itself. There are no clearance dimensions, warnings, or specific notes provided regarding the overhead electric lines on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1454,"outputTokens":629,"total