{"level":30,"time":1776272716047,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VSyp4M5CXCHd4P1meG3osU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting. The landscape plan shows:\n1. Overhead electric lines running horizontally along the southern edge\n2. Buildings set back significantly north\n3. Trees proposed near the southern OHE line\n4. No clearance dimensions shown\n5. No notes regarding overhead lines\n\nBut wait - from the existing conditions survey, the overhead lines were along the WESTERN property line (along Valley View Road), not the southern. Let me reconsider what I saw. The vision tool said on Sheet 31 they're showing at the \"bottom (southern)\" edge. But Sheet 31 is the landscape plan, and I need to understand the orientation better.\n\nActually, looking back at Sheet 4 description, it said the lines run North-South along Valley View Road, which is on the west. But the landscape plan shows lines at the \"southern edge.\" Let me visualize this better:\n\nValley View Road is on the west side of the property. So if lines run N-S along Valley View Road, they're on the western boundary. But the vision tool on Sheet 31 said the OHE runs \"horizontally across the very bottom (southern) edge.\" \n\nThis could mean:\na) There's another OHE line on the south side that I didn't catch on Sheet 4, or\nb) The vision tool is referring to the layout differently\n\nActually, wait - from the existing survey, there was also a \"West-to-East service drop line\" that crosses the property. This could be the line the vision tool is seeing on the landscape plan. The service drop would run west-to-east, and if we're looking at the landscape plan with a standard orientation (north up), a west-to-east line crossing the property from the western pole would appear to cross through the middle or lower part of the site.\n\nI should use the measure distance tool to get specific clearances if needed, but first let me read more of the site plan sheets to see if there are any elevation/section views showing clearances.\n\nLet me check Sheet 9 blocks to see if there's any detail about clearances, and also check the electrical plan (Sheet 21).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":50036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1083},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6450ffe4-612c-4eea-8b35-57aec9f3f591","uuid":"0a541e57-5702-4192-94f6-ed9a1693858b"}
