{"level":30,"time":1776272723756,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013F14i19QFwEBjdrZRZsx42","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of Site Plan Review - Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\nI have completed the evaluation of all 15 checklist items in Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). Here are my key findings:\n\n### Evidence Gathered:\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) clearly depicts overhead electric utility lines labeled \"-OHE-\" along the southern property boundary and \"-E-\" along the western boundary (Valley View Road)\n- Utility poles are shown at regular intervals along both lines\n- These are distribution-class lines (not transmission), indicated by voltage levels typical for standard overhead distribution\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\nSheet 35 (Plant Schedule) identifies four tree species:\n- Cedar Elm (10 trees, 100 gal., 16' minimum height)\n- Live Oak (2 trees, 100 gal., 16' minimum height)\n- Texas Mountain Laurel (2 trees, 45 gal., 8' minimum height)\n- Mexican Redbud (6 trees, 45 gal., 10' minimum height)\n\n**Critical Documentation Gaps:**\n- No utility-compatible (UC) status documented from ECM Appendix F for any species\n- No mature height verification against ECM Appendix F standards\n- No clearance dimensions from tree trunks to conductors or poles\n- No cross-reference between landscape plan and electrical infrastructure\n- No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted zones\n- Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan despite their 25-foot clearance requirement\n\n### Findings:\n\n**5 items marked as FAIL:**\n- **EL-2.3**: Large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) positioned within 25-foot clearance zone from distribution conductors\n- **EL-2.10**: Tree species not identified on landscape plan\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plan to verify clearances\n- **EL-2.14**: Relationship between proposed trees and overhead electric facilities not documented with clearances\n- **EL-2.15**: No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees within restricted zones\n\n**10 items marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE:**\nItems EL-2.1, 2.2, 2.4, 2.5, 2.6, 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 2.12, 2.13 cannot be assessed due to missing documentation, lack of dimensional references, or insufficient information on the plans.\n\nThe structured output has been provided with detailed deficiency statements, code citations, and applicable areas for each failing item."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3399,"cache_read_input_tokens":60551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3399},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3857099-05e9-4b26-b534-a07960b24bfd","uuid":"1c80a94d-07fb-46bf-80f0-33caed127ad2"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272723783,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":211034,"duration_api_ms":126465,"num_turns":20,"result":"## Summary of Site Plan Review - Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\nI have completed the evaluation of all 15 checklist items in Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). Here are my key findings:\n\n### Evidence Gathered:\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) clearly depicts overhead electric utility lines labeled \"-OHE-\" along the southern property boundary and \"-E-\" along the western boundary (Valley View Road)\n- Utility poles are shown at regular intervals along both lines\n- These are distribution-class lines (not transmission), indicated by voltage levels typical for standard overhead distribution\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\nSheet 35 (Plant Schedule) identifies four tree species:\n- Cedar Elm (10 trees, 100 gal., 16' minimum height)\n- Live Oak (2 trees, 100 gal., 16' minimum height)\n- Texas Mountain Laurel (2 trees, 45 gal., 8' minimum height)\n- Mexican Redbud (6 trees, 45 gal., 10' minimum height)\n\n**Critical Documentation Gaps:**\n- No utility-compatible (UC) status documented from ECM Appendix F for any species\n- No mature height verification against ECM Appendix F standards\n- No clearance dimensions from tree trunks to conductors or poles\n- No cross-reference between landscape plan and electrical infrastructure\n- No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted zones\n- Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan despite their 25-foot clearance requirement\n\n### Findings:\n\n**5 items marked as FAIL:**\n- **EL-2.3**: Large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) positioned within 25-foot clearance zone from distribution conductors\n- **EL-2.10**: Tree species not identified on landscape plan\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees not differentiated on plan to verify clearances\n- **EL-2.14**: Relationship between proposed trees and overhead electric facilities not documented with clearances\n- **EL-2.15**: No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees within restricted zones\n\n**10 items marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE:**\nItems EL-2.1, 2.2, 2.4, 2.5, 2.6, 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 2.12, 2.13 cannot be assessed due to missing documentation, lack of dimensional references, or insufficient information on the plans.\n\nThe structured output has been provided with detailed deficiency statements, code citations, and applicable areas for each failing item.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f3857099-05e9-4b26-b534-a07960b24bfd","total_cost_usd":0.18092515,"usage":{"input_tokens":121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41201,"cache_read_input_tokens":749879,"output_tokens":10863,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41201,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":121,"outputTokens":10863,"cacheReadInputTokens":749879,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41201,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18092515,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE utility line","Western property boundary along Valley View Road E utility line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan proposes Cedar Elm (typical mature height 50-70 feet) and Live Oak (typical mature height 40-50+ feet) trees within 25 feet of overhead electric distribution lines shown as -OHE- and -E- on the plan. Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are prohibited within 25 lateral feet of distribution conductors; no clearance dimensions, measurements, or variances are documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan areas near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) does not identify tree species at planting locations. While Sheet 35 provides a plant schedule listing species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud), the landscape plan itself shows only generic tree symbols (SY, PL, M designations) without species identification. Trees near overhead electric facilities must be identified by species on the landscape plan to verify utility compatibility and clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan areas near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape Plan does not differentiate large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) from smaller trees. All proposed trees near overhead electric infrastructure use the same symbol categories (SY, PL, M) without notation of mature height or large tree designation. Large trees near electric facilities must be clearly identified to verify compliance with 25-foot clearance requirements for distribution and 50-foot clearance for transmission."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire property; southern and western boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While Landscape Plan shows both proposed trees and overhead electric utility lines (-OHE- on southern boundary, -E- on western boundary), the relationship between trees and conductors is not clearly documented. No dimension lines, clearance callouts, notes, or cross-references indicate how trees comply with required clearances from overhead conductors and poles. Tree clearance compliance cannot be verified from the landscape plan as presented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE utility line","Western property boundary along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan in proximity to overhead electric distribution lines on both the southern and western boundaries. No documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing tree placement in restricted clearance zones is visible on the submitted plans. UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires explicit written approval from Austin Energy for variations to tree planting standards near electric facilities."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"955bde0b-c1a2-426b-9b39-d9acaa77d050"}
