{"level":30,"time":1776272739762,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WZSiaN4ACiyE2gK96SrVCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've reviewed the cover sheet blocks and there is NO note about the 48-hour notification requirement for work near high-voltage overhead lines. This is a required note per UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.\n\nNow I have a good overview. Let me summarize what I've found so far regarding the existence of overhead electric infrastructure on the site:\n\n**Applicability: YES - This grouping IS applicable**\n- The site has existing overhead electric lines and poles (confirmed by vision tool examination of Sheet 4 Existing Conditions Survey)\n- The site shows overhead electric lines on the landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n- The proposed development involves buildings, driveways, parking, etc. that may have clearance issues\n\n**Key Facts:**\n1. Existing overhead electric infrastructure:\n   - Utility poles along Valley View Road (western boundary) - at least 3 poles\n   - North-South main overhead line along the western property boundary\n   - West-to-East service drop line crossing the property to the former building\n   - Guy wires and anchors from poles\n\n2. Proposed development:\n   - 8 buildings (39 townhome units)\n   - Buildings appear to be set back from the western property line\n   - Driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks throughout the site\n   - Retaining walls\n   - Landscape plan shows mitigation trees near the OHE line\n\n**Key Missing Items Found So Far:**\n1. NO 48-hour notification note on cover sheet\n2. NO clearance dimensions shown on site plan or landscape plan for overhead lines\n3. NO profile/elevation views showing clearance verification\n4. NO survey data showing overhead conductor heights or mid-span clearances\n5. Landscape plan shows trees near OHE line but no clearance verification\n\nNow I need to systematically evaluate each checklist item. Let me organize my approach:\n\nFor each item, I'll check:\n- Is it applicable? (Does the condition exist on the site?)\n\n\n- If applicable, is there evidence of compliance?\n- If no evidence, what's the deficiency?\n\nI'll organize the evaluation by category: building clearances (EL-1.1, 1.3, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8), utility clearances (EL-1.28, 1.29), fences (EL-1.9, 1.10, 1.11, 1.12, 1.13), and retaining walls (EL-1.14, 1.15, 1.17).\n\nContinuing with driveways and parking areas (EL-1.18, 1.19, 1.20, 1.21), overhead line concerns (EL-1.22, 1.23, 1.24, 1.25, 1.26, 1.27), elevated structures (EL-1.5, 1.16), gas canopies (EL-1.4), vegetation (EL-1.37), and miscellaneous features (EL-1.2, 1.30 through 1.47).","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6419,"cache_read_input_tokens":57172,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6419},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6450ffe4-612c-4eea-8b35-57aec9f3f591","uuid":"3ef69865-68c7-4eaf-8215-2d4d9debcdec"}
