{"level":30,"time":1776272758844,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015ZcVyC1SLts6nAbB4hnTXH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have comprehensive information from Sheet 3. The notes show:\n\n**Electric Transmission Notes** (16 items):\n- No trees within 25 feet of transmission structure base\n- No digging/grading within 25 feet of transmission structures\n- 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting required with Austin Energy\n- 20-foot OSHA clearance from energized transmission lines\n- Warning signs must be placed under overhead transmission facilities\n- Various other requirements about access, fencing, fire hydrants, etc.\n\n**Electric Notes** (5 items):\n- Austin Energy right to prune/remove trees in easements\n- Developer must provide easements for electric facilities\n- Owner responsible for initial tree pruning within 10 feet of overhead facilities\n- Owner responsible for maintaining clearances (NESC, OSHA, COA, Texas law)\n- Relocation of electric facilities at landowner's expense\n\n**Critical Issue**: The notes refer to \"TRANSMISSION\" facilities and easements but:\n1. The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) showed **DISTRIBUTION** overhead utility lines (not transmission lines)\n2. Transmission typically >60kV; distribution is <60kV\n3. The notes address transmission, but the site has distribution lines\n\nI need to reconcile this discrepancy. Are the notes about transmission correct for this site, or do they incorrectly apply transmission requirements when the site actually has distribution lines?\n\nAlso, I still haven't seen if there are any specific notes about the DISTRIBUTION lines (the ones actually shown on Sheet 4) versus TRANSMISSION lines.\n\nLet me now create a comprehensive list of the findings and start evaluating each checklist item. Based on my research so far:\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH:**\n\n1. **Existing Facilities Confirmed**: Sheet 4 shows at least 3 utility poles and overhead utility lines (marked as \"- OH -\") running across the northern portion of the site (just inside the northern boundary), routing east-west.\n\n\n2. **Easement Constraints**: Two 5-foot electric easements bound the property on the north and east sides per the facts. The clearance dimensions from these overhead lines to proposed structures aren't dimensioned on Sheet 9, and I don't see building elevations with conductor data that would show vertical clearances either. The extensive transmission notes on Sheet 3 require a 48-hour pre-construction meeting and 20-foot OSHA clearances, but this conflicts with the distribution lines actually shown on the survey—I need to determine which requirements actually apply to this site.\n\n3. **Missing Distribution Line Notifications**: The transmission notes don't address the distribution overhead lines visible on the plans, so there's no specific cover sheet note requiring the 48-hour notice to Austin Energy before work near distribution conductors as mandated by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752 and UCM § 1.10.2. Additionally, no registered surveyor survey documenting pole locations and mid-span clearances appears in the submittal, and section views showing vertical clearance dimensions from conductors to roofs and driveways are absent.\n\nNow I need to work through the checklist systematically. The applicable items where overhead facilities are present include: EL-1.1 through EL-1.3 and EL-1.6 all require verification of clearance compliance, but EL-1.7 (conductor elevations on building sheets), EL-1.8 (section/plan views with dimensions), EL-1.23 (clearance measured from conductor, not pole), and EL-1.31 (registered surveyor data for pole locations and mid-span clearances) are not provided in the plans.\n\nAdditionally, EL-1.46 specifies a 48-hour notification requirement for distribution lines, which appears only for transmission lines here, and several other items depend on what specific features are actually depicted. I should evaluate all 47 checklist items to determine which fail, cannot be verified, or don't apply.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2719,"cache_read_input_tokens":62996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2719},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa426fab-05eb-4a3a-b7ff-045b4f6362f9","uuid":"cd3a3900-12d9-4028-84d2-fa3ddafba16b"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272759272,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan carefully to identify:\n\n1. **Overhead utility infrastructure**: Locate and note any overhead electric lines (labeled O.H.E., O.H.U.L., or similar) or utility poles shown on the plan.\n\n2. **Tree locations near overhead utilities**: Identify all trees (marked with symbols like \"+\", circles, or letters like \"SY\", \"PL\", \"P\", \"M\") that are located near the overhead electric lines. Note their approximate distances from the lines and poles.\n\n3. **Tree species identification**: Are tree species labels provided? Can you identify which specific trees are proposed near the overhead utilities?\n\n4. **Clearance dimensions**: Are there any dimension annotations or notes showing clearances between proposed trees and overhead conductors?\n\n5. **Utility-compatible tree markers**: Does the plan indicate which trees (if any) are utility-compatible (typically marked with \"UC\" designation per ECM Appendix F)?\n\n6. **Electric easement areas**: Are the electric easements shown, and do they contain any tree plantings?\n\nWhat trees are proposed within 10-50 feet of the overhead electric utilities, and are they verified as utility-compatible species?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Overhead utility infrastructure:**\nAn overhead electric line is clearly indicated along the bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan. The line is annotated repeatedly with \"- OHE -\". There are small circles with 'x' marks or crosshairs located along this line, which typically denote utility poles.\n\n**2. Tree locations near overhead utilities:**\nThere is a row of proposed trees located parallel to and just inside the property line/construction limits, directly adjacent to the \"- OHE -\" line along the southern boundary. Based on the provided graphic scale (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), these trees appear to be planted approximately 10 to 20 feet away from the overhead electric line. Several of these trees are denoted with the letter \"M\".\n\n**3. Tree species identification:**\nTree species labels are **not provided** on this sheet. There is no planting schedule or species legend present. The \"KEY NOTES\" section defines the letter designations by their functional role rather than species. For example:\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\nBecause there is no plant schedule on this page, the specific species proposed near the overhead utilities cannot be identified from this document alone.\n\n**4. Clearance dimensions:**\nThere are **no dimension annotations or notes** on this plan showing specific vertical or horizontal clearances between the proposed trees and the overhead conductors.\n\n**5. Utility-compatible tree markers:**\nThe plan **does not indicate** any utility-compatible tree markers. There are no \"UC\" designations in the Key Notes, nor are they appended to any of the tree symbols located near the \"- OHE -\" line.\n\n**6. Electric easement areas:**\nWhile the \"- OHE -\" line is clearly drawn, there are **no distinct lines labeled as Electric Easements or Public Utility Easements (P.U.E.)** delineated around the overhead lines on this specific sheet. The area where the trees are planted contains lines labeled \"- LOC -\" (Limits of Construction) and \"- SD -\" (Storm Drain), but no explicitly labeled electric easement area is visible.\n\n**Conclusion regarding your final question:**\nThere are multiple trees proposed within 10-50 feet (appearing to be roughly 10-20 feet) of the overhead electric utilities along the southern boundary. These trees are primarily labeled as \"M\" (Mitigation Trees). However, based solely on this sheet, **they cannot be verified as utility-compatible species** because the species are not listed, and there are no \"UC\" labels or specific utility clearance notes provided. You will need to refer to a planting schedule or tree list on a different sheet to determine their species and compatibility.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1558,"outputTokens":650,"totalTokens":4511,"reasoningTokens":2303},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan carefully to identify:\n\n1. **Overhead utility infrastructure**: Locate and note any overhead electric lines (labeled O.H.E., O.H.U.L., or similar) or utility poles shown on the plan.\n\n2. **Tree locations near overhead utilities**: Identify all trees (marked with symbols like \"+\", circles, or letters like \"SY\", \"PL\", \"P\", \"M\") that are located near the overhead electric lines. Note their approximate distances from the lines and poles.\n\n3. **Tree species identification**: Are tree species labels provided? Can you identify which specific trees are proposed near the overhead utilities?\n\n4. **Clearance dimensions**: Are there any dimension annotations or notes showing clearances between proposed trees and overhead conductors?\n\n5. **Utility-compatible tree markers**: Does the plan indicate which trees (if any) are utility-compatible (typically marked with \"UC\" designation per ECM Appendix F)?\n\n6. **Electric easement areas**: Are the electric easements shown, and do they contain any tree plantings?\n\nWhat trees are proposed within 10-50 feet of the overhead electric utilities, and are they verified as utility-compatible species?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-J9mm4FWrWxrhpzW9dOdYx2Wh","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"