ERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.3** - Building projections (overhangs, awnings, etc.) do not maintain clearances\n- Applicable? YES (buildings have roof overhangs/projections likely)\n\n\n- Evidence? NO - building elevations with clearance data are missing, so I can't verify projections meet requirements\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.4** - Gas pump canopies do not maintain clearances\n- Applicable? NO - no gas pump canopies proposed (residential townhomes)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.5** - Stairs, elevated walkways, platforms don't maintain 15-foot radial clearance\n- Applicable? MAYBE - elevated walkways might exist but I haven't seen details confirming this\n- Status: Need to verify if applicable\n\n**EL-1.6** - Buildings don't maintain clear ance from electric lines in ROW adjacent to site\n- Applicable? YES (buildings proposed, electric lines exist in/near Valley View Road ROW)\n- Evidence? NO specific clearances shown\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.7** - Surveyed elevations of overhead conductors not included on building elevation sheets\n- Applicable? YES (buildings proposed)\n- Evidence? NO building elevation sheets provided in the site plan\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE (no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor data)\n\n**EL-1.8** - Section and plan view exhibits don't show dimensions from conductor to building edges\n- Applicable? YES (buildings proposed, lines exist)\n- Evidence? NO section views showing clearance dimensions\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.9** - Fences do not maintain 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from conductors\n- Applicable? YES (site has fencing proposed)\n- Evidence? NO clearance dimensions shown between fence and conductors\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE (fences visible on survey and landscape plans but lack verification)\n\n**EL-1.10** - Fence posts do not maintain 10-foot clearance from poles\n- Applicable? YES (poles and fences both present)\n- Evidence? Specific post-to-pole distances not dimensioned\n- Status: POTENTIALLY FAIL (fence post locations relative to poles need verification)\n\n**EL-1.11** - Fences near substation not isolated with 10-foot non-conductive panel\n- Applicable? NO (no substation on site)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.12** - Fencing near transmission lines not non-conductive or grounded\n- Applicable? UNLIKELY (lines appear to be distribution voltage, not transmission)\n- Status: N/A pending voltage confirmation\n\n**EL-1.13** - Vehicle barrier fencing doesn't maintain 7.5-foot clearance\n- Applicable? UNLIKELY (no vehicle barrier visible under overhead lines)\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.14** - Retaining walls don't maintain 7.5-foot clearance from overhead lines\n- Applicable? YES (retaining walls shown on Sheet 38, overhead lines present)\n- Evidence? No clearance dimensions provided between walls and lines\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.15** - Retaining walls adjacent to substation don't maintain 5-foot separation\n- Applicable? NO (no substation on site)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.16** - Emergency access structures (bridges) don't maintain clearances\n- Applicable? NO (no bridges or emergency structures present)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.17** - Retaining wall sections lack clearance dimension exhibits\n- Applicable? YES (retaining walls proposed with overhead lines crossing)\n- Evidence? Sheet 38 shows sections but omits clearance dimensions from lines\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.18** - Driveways don't maintain vertical clearance (16 or 18 feet)\n- Applicable? YES (driveways shown on site plan with overhead lines crossing)\n- Evidence? No vertical clearance dimensions documented\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.19** - Vehicles parked on concrete pads don't maintain vertical clearance\n- Applicable? POSSIBLY (if parking areas fall beneath overhead lines)\n- Evidence? Parking areas shown but clearance not verified\n- Status: Need to determine if parking is positioned under lines\n\n**EL-\n\n1.20** - Roads/driveways don't maintain 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines\n- Applicable? UNLIKELY (lines appear to be distribution rather than transmission)\n- Status: N/A unless transmission lines are confirmed\n\n**EL-1.21** - Highway grades with underbuilt distribution don't maintain 40-foot clearance\n- Applicable? NO (no highway or freeway present)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.22** - Electric poles in conflict with proposed driveways not relocated 30 feet\n- Applicable? YES (poles exist along property boundary with driveways proposed)\n- Evidence? Site plan shows both poles and driveways; need to verify conflicts\n- Status: Requires specific conflict verification\n\n**EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions measured from pole instead of conductor\n- Applicable? YES (if clearance dimensions exist, must verify source point)\n- Evidence? No clearance dimensions provided\n- Status: FAIL - no clearance dimensions provided; any measurements shown appear to reference pole rather than conductor per site plan notes\n\n**EL-1.24** - Streetlight poles under overhead electric lines\n- Applicable? YES (streetlights shown on site plan)\n- Evidence? Need to verify streetlight placement relative to overhead lines\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.25** - Sidewalks not cleared from existing poles at property ends\n- Applicable? YES (sidewalks proposed at Valley View Road frontage near poles)\n- Evidence? Sidewalk proximity to poles shown but clearance not documented\n- Status: NOT-VERIFIABLE\n\n**EL-1.26** - Trash receptacles under overhead lines\n- Applicable? YES (trash enclosures shown on landscape plan)\n- Evidence? Need to check trash enclosure placement relative to overhead lines\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.27** - Facilities installed under/over overhead distribution in violation\n- Applicable? YES (proposed buildings and structures; overhead lines traverse property)\n- Evidence? Site plan indicates building locations and line routing; must verify if structures sit directly beneath lines\n- Status: Requires verification based on routing\n\n**EL-1.28** - Water meters don't maintain clearance from overhead service drops\n- Applicable? YES (water service and drops shown on utility plan)\n- Evidence? Water meter locations need review on utility documentation\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.29** - Water lines don't maintain clearance from overhead distribution\n- Applicable? YES (water lines indicated on plans)\n- Evidence? Must check for conflicts between water line routing and overhead lines\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.30** - Foundations within 5 feet of property line don't allow electric facility clearance space\n- Applicable? YES (buildings positioned near property lines with potential electric facilities in ROW)\n- Evidence? Site plan shows building setbacks and property boundaries; specific distances need verification\n- Status: Requires verification\n\n**EL-1.31** - Survey not provided showing vertical clearances when insufficient\n- Applicable? YES (vertical clearances appear marginal from available estimates)\n- Evidence? No registered surveyor documentation exists for mid-span clearance measurements\n- Status: FAIL - survey of overhead facility elevations and clearances not provided\n\n**EL-1.32** - Overhead lines don't cross roads at 90-degree angle\n- Applicable? NO - no new overhead lines crossing proposed roads\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.33** - Secondary lines cross over primary lines\n- Applicable? NO - secondary/primary crossing unlikely (service drop over main line is standard)\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.34** - Marquee signs lack clearance verification\n- Applicable? NO - no marquee signs present\n- Status: N/A\n\n**EL-1.35** - New power poles for underground service less than 20 feet from existing poles\n- Applicable? POSSIBLY - development includes new electrical service\n- Evidence? Sheet 21 shows underground service, but whether new poles are actually proposed remains unclear\n- Status: Need to verify\n\n**EL-1.36*