{"level":30,"time":1776272817880,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01L7uAV2uRikdwoMzWMSQmTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect - my findings are confirmed. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan):\n1. Does NOT provide cross-references to the plant list on Sheet 35\n2. Does NOT include a legend with species names\n3. Does NOT label trees with species abbreviations\n4. Does NOT identify the species of the Mitigation Trees in the bottom right corner\n\nThis is a clear deficiency for EL-2.10: \"Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities\"\n\nNow let me also check on EL-2.11: \"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) not differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities\"\n\nSince:\n1. The plant list on Sheet 35 shows minimum planting sizes (16' HT, 8' HT, 10' HT) but these are NOT the mature heights\n2. The landscape plan shows trees only as symbols without any indication of which are large trees\n3. Live Oak and Cedar Elm are likely to have mature heights of 40+ feet based on ECM Appendix F standards\n4. There is no way to distinguish on the landscape plan between large trees (40+ ft mature) and small trees (< 40 ft mature)\n\nThis is a deficiency for EL-2.11.\n\nNow, for items EL-2.1 and EL-2.3, I need to determine if the trees shown near the overhead electric lines can have their compliance verified. Since:\n1. The species of trees near the OHE lines cannot be determined from the landscape plan\n2. The mature heights cannot be determined from the landscape plan\n3. No clearance dimensions are shown on the plan\n\nItems EL-2.1 and EL-2.3 cannot be verified - they are \"not-verifiable\" status because the required information (species and mature height of trees near overhead facilities) is missing from the plans.\n\nLet me now think about the other items systematically. Let me create a checklist based on my research:\n\n\nEL-2.1 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot determine species)\nEL-2.2 - Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission - STATUS: NOT-APPLICABLE (no transmission lines identified)\nEL-2.3 - Large trees within 25 ft of distribution - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot determine species/mature height)\nEL-2.4 - Large trees within 50 ft of transmission - STATUS: NOT-APPLICABLE (no transmission lines)\nEL-2.5 - Trees within transmission easement - STATUS: NOT-APPLICABLE (no transmission easement on site)\nEL-2.6 - Trees within 10 ft of overhead poles - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (poles not shown on landscape plan)\nEL-2.7 - Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (pad-mounts not shown on landscape plan)\nEL-2.8 - Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (underground equipment locations not shown on landscape plan)\nEL-2.9 - Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lack root barriers - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot determine distances and root barrier specs not shown)\nEL-2.10 - Plant legend/schedule doesn't identify species near electric facilities - STATUS: FAIL\nEL-2.11 - Large trees not differentiated on plans - STATUS: FAIL\nEL-2.12 - Clear\nEL-2.13 - Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor - STATUS: N/A (no clearances dimensioned)\nEL-2.14 - Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk - STATUS: N/A (no clearances dimensioned)\nEL-2.15 - Trees shown in relation to overhead facilities - STATUS: PASS (both are shown)\nEL-2.16 - Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval - STATUS: NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot determine without species/distance data)\n\nI need to verify whether overhead electric facilities actually exist on this site to determine if this entire section applies. Looking at Sheet 31, I can see overhead electric lines marked as \"OHE\" running along the bottom edge of the landscape plan.\n\nFour mitigation trees are positioned near these lines, though the landscape plan doesn't identify them by species. This confirms the grouping is applicable since overhead electric infrastructure is present on the site.\n\nThe lines appear to be distribution rather than transmission—no labeling indicates transmission voltage, and the regulatory guidance notes that typical development sites have distribution facilities unless explicitly marked otherwise.\n\nBased on this analysis, the key deficiencies are: EL-2.10 fails because tree species aren't identified in the legend or schedule, and EL-2.11 fails because large trees aren't differentiated to verify clearances. EL-2.1 cannot be verified without knowing the specific species proposed near the electric facilities.\n\nSeveral other items also cannot be verified: EL-2.3 lacks species and mature height data needed to confirm large tree compliance; EL-2.6 cannot be assessed because utility poles aren't shown relative to trees on the landscape plan; EL-2.8 and EL-2.9 cannot be verified because underground equipment locations and distances aren't correlated to the landscape plan, and root barrier specifications are missing. EL-2.15 cannot be verified without species and distance information, plus no Austin Energy approval letter was provided.\n\nI should double-check whether the electrical design plan shows poles and underground equipment locations that could help verify EL-2.6, EL-2.8, and EL-2.9.\n\nThe landscape plan should display all relevant utilities—including poles, pad-mounts, and underground equipment—so tree placement can be compared against clearance requirements. Since these items aren't shown in a way that allows verification, the compliance cannot be confirmed. This reflects a fundamental issue with plan coordination: all utilities affecting tree placement need to be visible on the landscape plan itself.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2697,"cache_read_input_tokens":59426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2697},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"bd98048f-aa3e-4c6d-a144-700c66cd66b3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272817880,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01L7uAV2uRikdwoMzWMSQmTp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan, I can now compile my findings. Let me document what I've found:\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Site Infrastructure Identified:**\n- Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) running along the bottom south edge of the property\n- Proposed trees include 20 total trees: 2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, 6 Mexican Redbud\n- Four Mitigation trees (marked \"M\") are shown in the bottom right corner of the site, in proximity to the overhead electric line\n\n**Critical Finding - Missing Information:**\n- The Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows trees ONLY by category symbol (M, SY, PL, P = Mitigation, Street Yard, Parking Lot, Parking Buffer)\n- NO plant schedule legend appears on the Landscape Plan that identifies tree species by symbol\n- NO cross-reference to Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations) plant list exists on the Landscape Plan\n- Therefore, the species of ANY trees shown on the landscape plan, including those near the overhead electric lines, CANNOT be determined from the landscape plan documents\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Species identification for trees near overhead electric facilities (items EL-2.1, 2.3, 2.10)\n- Mature heights for proposed trees per ECM Appendix F (items EL-2.3, 2.11)\n- Utility pole locations shown on landscape plan in relation to trees (item EL-2.6)\n- Pad-mounted equipment shown on landscape plan (item EL-2.7)\n- Underground equipment locations shown on landscape plan with clearances to trees (items EL-2.8, 2.9)\n- Any cross-reference or linking between the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) regarding utility equipment and tree locations\n- Documentation of Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted zones (item EL-2.15)\n- Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment (item EL-2.9)\n\n## Checklist Item Evaluations\n\n**EL-2.1**: Cannot verify - requires species identification not available on landscape plan  \n**EL-2.3**: Cannot verify - requires species and mature height data not available on landscape plan  \n**EL-2.6**: Cannot verify - poles not shown on landscape plan relative to trees  \n**EL-2.8**: Cannot verify - underground equipment locations not shown on landscape plan  \n**EL-2.9**: Cannot verify - distances and root barrier specs not available  \n**EL-2.10**: FAIL - Trees near overhead electric facilities are shown only as category symbols without species identification  \n**EL-2.11**: FAIL - No indication on landscape plan of which trees are large (40+ ft mature height)  \n**EL-2.14**: PASS - Overhead electric lines AND trees are shown on landscape plan  \n**EL-2.15**: Cannot verify - cannot determine prohibited zones without species/height data, and no Austin Energy approval found  \n\nNow let me return the structured findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2697,"cache_read_input_tokens":59426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2697},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"6931aa0f-4e86-46d1-b7ba-68fb78575943"}
