{"level":30,"time":1776272817880,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JRNefEBn929NvpHk5bmmHp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've successfully completed the site plan review for grouping EL-2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\nSummary of my findings:\n- 2 FAIL items: EL-2.10 and EL-2.11\n- 6 NOT-VERIFIABLE items: EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.6, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.15\n\nThe main issues are:\n1. Trees are shown on the landscape plan using only category symbols (M, SY, PL, P) with no plant schedule legend identifying species\n2. Large trees (40+ ft mature height) are not differentiated on the plans\n3. Various utility locations (poles, underground equipment) are not shown on the landscape plan to enable clearance verification\n4. No Austin Energy written approval documented for any trees in restricted zones\n\nThe root cause is a lack of integration between the electrical design plan (Sheet 21) showing electrical infrastructure and the landscape plan (Sheet 31) showing tree locations. There's also missing information about tree species and mature heights on the landscape plan itself.\n\nAll findings have been properly formatted and submitted through the StructuredOutput tool with appropriate code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and comment text.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4546,"cache_read_input_tokens":62123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4546},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"0637ca87-c34e-4ffd-a863-34862070bcc3"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272817880,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JRNefEBn929NvpHk5bmmHp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Applicable Scope:** This grouping applies to the Valley View Townhomes project because overhead electric lines (OHE) are present and depicted on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) running along the south property boundary. Four mitigation trees are shown on the landscape plan in proximity to these overhead electric lines.\n\n**Key Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)**: The landscape plan shows trees only by category symbols (M, SY, PL, P) with no plant schedule legend or species identification. The four mitigation trees near the overhead electric lines cannot be identified by species, preventing verification of utility-compatibility requirements.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)**: Large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape plan. The plan shows all trees using identical category symbols without any notation of mature height or size classification.\n\n3. **EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.15 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Species identification and mature heights are required to verify that trees near overhead conductors comply with clearance distances. Because these fundamental data are absent from the landscape plan, compliance cannot be verified.\n\n4. **EL-2.6, EL-2.8, EL-2.9 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Utility pole and underground equipment locations are not shown on the landscape plan (though they appear on Sheet 21 electrical design plan), preventing verification of clearances from trees. Root barrier specifications are also not provided.\n\n**Root Cause:** The landscape plan lacks integration with the electrical infrastructure shown on the electrical design plan. Trees are identified by category only, with no connection to the species and maturity information on Sheet 35. This prevents verification of compliance with UCM § 1.10.10.4 clearance requirements.\n\n**Required Corrections:**\n- Add species identification to the landscape plan (via legend, plant schedule, or annotation)\n- Differentiate large trees (40+ feet) on the landscape plan\n- Overlay electrical infrastructure (poles, equipment, underground lines) onto the landscape plan, or provide clear cross-references\n- Clarify mature heights per ECM Appendix F for all trees\n- Document any Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted zones\n\nAll findings have been submitted in the structured format."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4546,"cache_read_input_tokens":62123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4546},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d1a7ac5-a447-4e3a-aebe-824ab80a6536","uuid":"59eeed9f-c4f1-4eba-8a31-5a5d1352ef0b"}
