1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed water and wastewater lines are shown on utility tap plans, but no dimension annotations or profile views show clearance distances from these lines to existing overhead electrical distribution facilities and poles on the southern boundary. Dimension annotations on utility plan showing clearance distances from overhead pole locations to water/wastewater line routing required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 near southern property line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings 7 and 8 are proposed within 30-50 feet of the southern property line where existing overhead electric facilities are located. No documentation confirms that permanent structure foundations maintain sufficient clearance (typically 5 feet minimum from property line) to allow adequate clearance space for electric facilities and infrastructure. Verification of foundation setbacks from property line and coordination with utility clearance requirements needed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8; southern driveway and parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearances from proposed site features (buildings, driveways) to overhead electric lines appear potentially marginal based on site plan data and existing overhead line routing shown on southern boundary. No registered surveyor data showing pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearances is provided to verify that minimum 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearances (horizontal) and 16-18 foot vertical clearances (for driveways) are maintained. Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey with conductor elevation data required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Exterior decorative lighting throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed decorative landscape lighting is shown on site plan and landscape plan in proximity to overhead electric lines on southern boundary. No dimension annotations or clearance verification are provided confirming that decorative light fixtures maintain the required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from outside electric conductors, or noting relocation. Clearance dimensions or relocation notes for decorative lighting near overhead lines required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary where trees are proposed near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed new trees (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak, 6 Mexican Redbud, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel) are shown planted approximately 10-20 feet from the overhead electric line on the southern boundary (Sheet 31). No utility-compatible (UC) species designations are provided on the landscape plan, and no documentation confirms species comply with ECM Appendix F utility-compatible requirements. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are typically NOT utility-compatible species for distribution lines due to mature height exceeding 20 feet. Landscape plan must clearly mark all trees near overhead utilities with UC designations, species verified against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list, and minimum 10-foot lateral distance confirmed for distribution (50 feet for transmission)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric meter locations are shown on the preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21), but no enlarged details or obstruction verification is provided confirming that meters are not obstructed by buildings, fences, landscaping, or other site features. Working clearance requirements (30-inch wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9) cannot be verified. Enlarged detail drawings showing meter locations with clearance zones and obstruction verification required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 7 and 8 near existing streetlights"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight poles may be located at property boundaries along Valley View Road. Proposed buildings are shown on the site plan, but no dimension annotations or clearance verification is provided confirming required clearances from buildings to existing streetlight poles. Dimension annotations showing building-to-pole clearances, or confirmation that streetlights do not conflict with proposed structures, required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed driveways and accessible paths throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires (support cables from poles to ground anchors) from existing distribution poles on the property boundary may conflict with proposed accessible paths and driveways shown on the site plan. The existing conditions survey shows guy anchors at several poles, but these are frequently omitted from or unclear on proposed plans. No notation or detail confirms whether down guy anchor points and guy wire routing are resolved through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting structures. Verification that proposed paths and driveways avoid guy wire conflicts required; if conflicts exist, note resolution method (pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting pole)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted transformers and equipment on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted transformer equipment is shown on the site plan and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) but located in proximity to existing overhead electric lines on the southern boundary (based on overhead line routing shown). No vertical clearance dimensions are provided from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment. Section view showing vertical clearance from outside conductor to top of transformer required to verify minimum 7.5-foot clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas and equipment operation zones throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Erosion and sedimentation control plan (Sheet 5) shows construction limits and potential staging areas near overhead electric lines on the southern boundary. No documentation confirms that construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms maintain the minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines as required by OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2. This is distinct from permanent clearance requirements. Construction logistics plan with 10-foot radial clearance zone marked around overhead utilities required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general site plan notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"High-voltage overhead electric lines exist on and adjacent to the site. No plan note is provided requiring that owner/contractor notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines as mandated by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. Required 48-hour notification note must be added to cover sheet or general notes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Electric service mast locations at buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Service mast locations connecting to the underground electrical service are indicated on the site plan and electrical design plan but building elevations showing service mast through-roof installations, roof clearance dimensions, and distance from roof edge are not provided. Building elevation sheets with service mast locations, clearance dimensions (minimum 3-foot above roof, or 18-inch if within 4 feet of roof edge), and voltage designation (≤300V applicability) required."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4489,"cache_read_input_tokens":68489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4489},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b9758a-7404-4795-a19d-c8c5d3a54014","uuid":"97557f66-aefb-4140-a176-d006a9c7da46"}
