{"level":30,"time":1776272943324,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01R4J6XzLzvVBW32gFrDR2TP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've successfully completed the site plan review for grouping 1 (EL-md-exp/1.md) and returned the structured output with all the fail and not-verifiable findings.\n\nLet me summarize what I found:\n\n**GROUPING 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines - FINDINGS SUMMARY**\n\n**Applicability:** APPLICABLE - Overhead electric facilities exist on the property boundary\n\n**Infrastructure Confirmed:**\n- 5 overhead electric poles with guy anchors along property perimeter\n- Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) running along three sides of property\n- Multiple electric easements (5-ft and 10-ft widths)\n- Existing overhead distribution facilities on southern boundary\n\n**Proposed Site Features in Clearance Zone:**\n- Buildings 7-8 (southern portion)\n- Southern driveway loop and parking areas\n- Proposed trees (12 new trees of various species)\n- Fences, retaining walls, and utilities\n\n**FINDINGS OVERVIEW:**\n\n**FAIL Items (2):**\n1. EL-1.8 - Section/profile exhibits showing clearance dimensions completely absent\n2. EL-1.23 - No clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (measured from pole instead, or missing entirely)\n3. EL-1.37 - Proposed trees near overhead utilities not verified as utility-compatible; Cedar Elm and Live Oak are NOT utility-compatible\n4. EL-1.46 - No 48-hour Austin Energy notification note on plans\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items (24):**\n- EL-1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.6, 1.7 (Building clearances not documented)\n- EL-1.9, 1.10, 1.13, 1.14, 1.17 (Fence/wall clearances not documented)\n- EL-1.18, 1.19 (Driveway/parking vertical clearances not verified)\n\n\n- EL-1.22, 1.24-1.31 (Various feature clearances including utilities and site elements lack documentation)\n- EL-1.36, 1.38-1.40 (Lighting, meters, streetlight, and guy wire clearances not documented)\n- EL-1.43, 1.45, 1.47 (Transformer, construction staging, and service mast clearances not documented)\n\nThe review identified significant gaps in overhead electric utility clearance documentation across multiple site features and infrastructure elements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9570,"cache_read_input_tokens":72978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9570},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b9758a-7404-4795-a19d-c8c5d3a54014","uuid":"9b9ec5cb-dba8-4e7f-aeb5-dd227b609da8"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272943324,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01R4J6XzLzvVBW32gFrDR2TP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete - Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 1** covering clearance requirements for overhead electric facilities and proposed site features.\n\n### Key Findings Summary:\n\n**Applicability: CONFIRMED APPLICABLE**\n- Overhead electric poles and conductors (O.H.U.L.) exist on the property perimeter (southern boundary and two other sides)\n- Multiple overhead poles with guy anchors identified at property boundaries\n- Existing electric easements documented (5-ft and 10-ft widths)\n- Proposed buildings, driveways, parking, and features located in proximity to these overhead utilities\n\n### Critical Deficiencies Identified:\n\n**FAIL Items (4 deficiencies):**\n1. **EL-1.8** - Section/plan exhibits showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to buildings and site features are completely absent\n2. **EL-1.23** - No clearance dimensions provided from outside conductor (fundamental measurement requirement violated)\n3. **EL-1.37** - Proposed trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) near overhead utilities are NOT verified as utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F\n4. **EL-1.46** - Required 48-hour Austin Energy notification note missing from plans\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items (24 deficiencies):**\nClearance compliance cannot be verified for:\n- Buildings 7-8 horizontal/vertical clearances from conductors\n- Building projections (roof eaves, overhangs)\n- Fences and retaining walls\n- Driveway and parking vertical clearances (16-18 ft requirement)\n- Proposed trees (species and clearances)\n- Transformers and electrical equipment\n- Water meters and utility lines\n- Landscaping and decorative lighting\n- Construction staging areas\n- Service mast clearances\n\n### Root Cause:\nThe applicant has submitted plans showing overhead electric facilities (labeled \"OHE\" on site plan) but **failed to provide any clearance dimension annotations, surveyed conductor elevations, profile sections, or utility-compatible tree verification.** This represents a systematic gap in the required clearance documentation per UCM § 1.10.3.\n\n---\n\nThe structured output has been generated with **28 findings** (4 fail + 24 not-verifiable) documenting each deficiency with specific code citations, applicable areas, and required remediation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9570,"cache_read_input_tokens":72978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9570},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0b9758a-7404-4795-a19d-c8c5d3a54014","uuid":"6dfbdcf4-ce90-46f7-95b0-44762dbce27d"}
