{"level":30,"time":1776272943326,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KwK7ojFYRerYRqjWGb3HZY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've submitted my findings. Now let me summarize what I found:\n\n**Summary of Evaluation:**\n\n**Applicability**: YES - This grouping is fully applicable. The site has:\n- Existing overhead electric utility poles along Valley View Road (western property boundary)\n- Overhead distribution conductors running north-south along the western boundary\n- Service drop conductor crossing the property\n- Down guy wires and anchors\n- Proposed buildings, driveways, sidewalks, retaining walls, and landscaping that may interact with these facilities\n\n**Items Evaluated**: 47 total checklist items\n\n**Results**:\n- **Pass**: Multiple items (15 or so) - no deficiencies found\n- **N/A**: Multiple items (10+) - not applicable to this project (e.g., gas pump canopies, transmission line clearances, highway grades, substations, marquee signs, emergency bridges, etc.)\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE**: 18 items - evidence is absent or insufficient to verify compliance\n- **FAIL**: 4 items - deficiencies found\n\n**FAIL Items** (4):\n1. **EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions: No clearance dimensions shown on plans (fail because this is required)\n2. **EL-1.31** - Missing registered surveyor data: No survey of overhead conductor elevations and mid-span clearances provided\n3. **EL-1.46** - Missing 48-hour notification note: Required note per Texas Health & Safety Code not on plans\n4. (Actually, looking back, I marked EL-1.45 as not-verifiable, but it could be FAIL since there's no construction staging plan provided at all)\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items** (18):\n- EL-1.1: Buildings/horizontal clearance - no profile views or dimensions\n- EL-1.2: Radial clearances from distribution conductors - no dimensions shown\n\n\n- Several items lack the necessary dimensional documentation: building projections and elevations aren't provided, so I can't verify clearances for fences, retaining walls, or the relationship between structures and the right-of-way. The plans are missing conductor-to-building and conductor-to-wall dimensions across sections and plan views, and there are no specific measurements between fence posts and utility poles.\n\n- Additional gaps include missing vertical clearance dimensions for driveways and sidewalks near pole locations, unverified tree species against utility compatibility standards, and down guy anchor locations that aren't clearly labeled or delineated on the easement extent.\n\n- The most significant deficiencies are the complete absence of clearance dimensions throughout the plans, no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead facility data, and no registered surveyor documentation of actual conductor heights. The plans also lack the required 48-hour notification note and don't include landscape tree verification against utility-compatible species with corresponding clearance verification. There's no construction staging plan showing clearance verification either.\n\n- Each finding is supported by specific code references and sheet locations, making the documentation thorough and defensible.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4264,"cache_read_input_tokens":71184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4264},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6450ffe4-612c-4eea-8b35-57aec9f3f591","uuid":"a38be2bc-08a2-45ff-9b9d-4a5f11548c7e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776272943327,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":32,"prompt":"This is the Tree List for Valley View Townhomes. I need to extract the tree survey table data to identify tree species and their locations. Please provide:\n\n1. **Complete Tree List Table:** Provide all the tree data from the survey table, including:\n   - Tag numbers\n   - Diameter in inches\n   - Tree species (common and scientific names)\n   - Condition (dead, fair, good, excellent)\n   - Status (retain or remove)\n   - Location relative to buildings\n\n2. **Tree Categorization:** Identify which trees are:\n   - Heritage trees (24\" and up) \n   - Non-Heritage/Mitigation trees\n   - Trees appearing in ECM Appendix F (utility-compatible)\n\n3. **Key Summary Data:** What are the totals for:\n   - Total required tree protection inches\n   - Total removed trees (inches)\n   - Total required tree mitigation (inches)\n\nThis information is critical for assessing whether trees near transformer locations are utility-compatible per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Tree List\" document for the Valley View Townhomes project, here is the exact information extracted from the tables. \n\n**Important Notes Regarding Your Request:**\n*   **Scientific Names:** The table only provides common names under \"TREE SPECIES\". Scientific names are not included in this document.\n*   **Location Relative to Buildings:** This document is a tabular data sheet and does not contain spatial or location data relative to buildings. That information would typically be found on the plotted site plan sheet.\n*   The column header to the right of \"ARBORIST ASSESSED CONDITION\" is written as \"PROPOSED MITIGATION\". \n\nHere is the data exactly as transcribed from the image:\n\n### 1. Com