{"level":30,"time":1776272943330,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Jdp49JEUGExPSy6EaKBqZ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 Site Plan, here is the information regarding the overhead electric lines (designated by the line type **\"- OHE -\"**) and their relationship to proposed structures and features:\n\n**1. Which buildings (1-8) appear to be closest to the overhead electric line(s)? What is the approximate horizontal distance?**\n\nThere are two distinct overhead electric line routes visible on the perimeter of the site: one running along the Southern boundary line and one running along the Eastern boundary line.\n\n*   **Closest to the Eastern OHE line:** **Bldg. 6** is the closest. Using the visual 1\" = 20' scale provided, the eastern-most edge of Bldg. 6 appears to be approximately **15 to 20 feet** horizontally from the OHE line running along the eastern property boundary.\n*   **Closest to the Southern OHE line:** **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are the closest. Based on the visual scale, the southern facades of these buildings appear to be approximately **35 to 45 feet** horizontally from the OHE line running along the southern boundary.\n\n**2. What site features (driveways, parking, retaining walls, sidewalks, etc.) appear to be closest to the overhead lines?**\n\n*   **Southern OHE Line:**\n    *   **Driveway:** The line crosses directly over the main southern entrance, labeled **\"Construct Type III / Driveway / See Detail 4/335-2\"**.\n    *   **Retaining Walls:** A wall labeled **\"Concrete Retaining / Wall\"** runs closely parallel to the OHE line along the southern boundary.\n    *   **Sidewalk:** The proposed sidewalk running parallel to the southern driveway passes near the line.\n*   **Eastern OHE Line:**\n    *   **Retaining Walls:** A long retaining wall runs parallel and very close to the eastern OHE line. Sections are labeled **\"Concrete / Retaining Wall\"** and **\"Existing Retaining / Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n    *   **Fencing:** A line labeled **\"Wood Fence\"** runs closely parallel to the OHE line.\n    *   **Recreation Area:** An area with a **\"BBQ Pit\"** and **\"Gravel\"** near Bldg. 5 sits in close proximity to the eastern line.\n    *   **Drainage:** A **\"Drainage Easement\"** outfall path passes under/near the line at the southeast corner.\n\n**3. Are there any dimension lines, annotations, or clearance labels visible on the site plan related to the overhead utilities?**\n\n*   There are **no explicit clearance dimension lines** (e.g., showing a required 10-foot or 15-foot safety buffer zone) drawn between the overhead lines and the proposed buildings.\n*   There are **no annotations** explicitly stating required horizontal or vertical clearance requirements from the overhead lines.\n*   There are annotations denoting legal utility easements near the Eastern OHE line, specifically:\n    *   **\"5' Elec. Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement / Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 / D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"3' Electric Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**4. Do the buildings, driveways, or structures appear to pass directly beneath or be potentially too close to the overhead line routing?**\n\n*   **Passing directly beneath:** Yes. The main southern driveway entrance (**\"Construct Type III / Driveway\"**) and adjacent sidewalk pass directly beneath the southern OHE line.\n*   **Buildings passing beneath:** No proposed buildings (Bldg. 1-8) pass directly underneath the overhead lines.\n*   **Potentially too close:** While \"too close\" depends on specific utility regulations and line voltages not provided on this sheet, the following areas represent tight constraints:\n    *   The extensive **retaining walls** along both the southern and eastern boundaries appear to be sited almost directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the overhead line routing. Construction activities (excavation, equipment operation) for these walls would occur in very close proximity to the lines.\n    *   **Bldg. 6** is the tightest building constraint, sitting visually ~15-20 feet from the eastern pole line. Depending on conductor swing under wind load, this may require verification against local utility clearance standards."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa426fab-05eb-4a3a-b7ff-045b4f6362f9","uuid":"7ea4597b-325e-44e9-8afc-542b109de9aa","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 Site Plan, here is the information regarding the overhead electric lines (designated by the line type **\"- OHE -\"**) and their relationship to proposed structures and features:\n\n**1. Which buildings (1-8) appear to be closest to the overhead electric line(s)? What is the approximate horizontal distance?**\n\nThere are two distinct overhead electric line routes visible on the perimeter of the site: one running along the Southern boundary line and one running along the Eastern boundary line.\n\n*   **Closest to the Eastern OHE line:** **Bldg. 6** is the closest. Using the visual 1\" = 20' scale provided, the eastern-most edge of Bldg. 6 appears to be approximately **15 to 20 feet** horizontally from the OHE line running along the eastern property boundary.\n*   **Closest to the Southern OHE line:** **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 8** are the closest. Based on the visual scale, the southern facades of these buildings appear to be approximately **35 to 45 feet** horizontally from the OHE line running along the southern boundary.\n\n**2. What site features (driveways, parking, retaining walls, sidewalks, etc.) appear to be closest to the overhead lines?**\n\n*   **Southern OHE Line:**\n    *   **Driveway:** The line crosses directly over the main southern entrance, labeled **\"Construct Type III / Driveway / See Detail 4/335-2\"**.\n    *   **Retaining Walls:** A wall labeled **\"Concrete Retaining / Wall\"** runs closely parallel to the OHE line along the southern boundary.\n    *   **Sidewalk:** The proposed sidewalk running parallel to the southern driveway passes near the line.\n*   **Eastern OHE Line:**\n    *   **Retaining Walls:** A long retaining wall runs parallel and very close to the eastern OHE line. Sections are labeled **\"Concrete / Retaining Wall\"** and **\"Existing Retaining / Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n    *   **Fencing:** A line labeled **\"Wood Fence\"** runs closely parallel to the OHE line.\n    *   **Recreation Area:** An area with a **\"BBQ Pit\"** and **\"Gravel\"** near Bldg. 5 sits in close proximity to the eastern line.\n    *   **Drainage:** A **\"Drainage Easement\"** outfall path passes under/near the line at the southeast corner.\n\n**3. Are there any dimension lines, annotations, or clearance labels visible on the site plan related to the overhead utilities?**\n\n*   There are **no explicit clearance dimension lines** (e.g., showing a required 10-foot or 15-foot safety buffer zone) drawn between the overhead lines and the proposed buildings.\n*   There are **no annotations** explicitly stating required horizontal or vertical clearance requirements from the overhead lines.\n*   There are annotations denoting legal utility easements near the Eastern OHE line, specifically:\n    *   **\"5' Elec. Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement / Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 / D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   **\"3' Electric Easement / Vol. 69, Pg. 14 / Vol. 73, Pg. 76 / P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**4. Do the buildings, driveways, or structures appear to pass directly beneath or be potentially too close to the overhead line routing?**\n\n*   **Passing directly beneath:** Yes. The main southern driveway entrance (**\"Construct Type III / Driveway\"**) and adjacent sidewalk