elecom:** A \"3' Electric Easement\" is labeled along the eastern boundary near Bldg. 6. A \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" is visible running along the southern boundary line.\n*   **General/Other:** \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" is noted on the eastern edge; a \"Sidewalk Easement\" is on the western frontage.\n\n**8. Retaining walls**\nRetaining walls are extensively used around the perimeter of the site to manage grade changes:\n*   **North:** Labeled **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** north of Bldg. 3.\n*   **East:** A **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** encloses the \"Detention Pond\" in the northeast. Behind Bldgs. 5 and 6 on the eastern property line, there is an **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n*   **South:** Labels for **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** and **\"Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\"** are located along the southern property line behind Bldgs. 8, 7, and 6.\n*   **West:** A **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** label is visible at the southwest corner near Bldg. 8.\n\n**9. Overall site organization**\nThe site is a rectangular parcel organized with a high-density, multi-family townhome layout. The 8 building clusters are oriented inward toward a central loop drive aisle system that provides garage access to residents. The site utilizes the perimeter for infrastructure and amenities, tucking a detention pond into the northeast corner, wrapping the north, east, and south edges with retaining walls and a decomposed granite walking trail, and concentrating most of the existing/proposed tree canopy along these outer boundaries to act as a buffer. The western edge serves as the sole vehicular entry point and primary utility connection hub."}]}
