{"level":30,"time":1776273026252,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015pqFtsg8JpaU47HSB9tzDn","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 23 — Construction Details 2\n     2→\n     3→Standard construction details for water infrastructure, valves, and fire hydrants.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains \"Construction Details 2\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, specifically focusing on City of Austin standard details. It provides specifications, cross-sections, and installation procedures for typical gate valves (4\"-16\"), fire hydrant assemblies, and utility trenching with unfinished surfaces.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Gate Valves:**\n    11→    *   Clearance: 3\" - 5\"\n    12→    *   Concrete Block (for valves <12\"): 16\" x 16\" x 4\" minimum\n    13→    *   Concrete cradle: Minimum 2000 P.S.I., Class B\n    14→    *   Concrete pad patch: 3' x 3' minimum (Item 403S Class \"A\") with 5\" minimum depth and #5 rebar at mid-depth.\n    15→    *   Total depth of asphalt + concrete: 9\" minimum\n    16→    *   Stem extensions required when valves exceed 3' deep from finished grade; extension nut must be 12\" - 18\" from finished grade.\n    17→    *   Valve component weights: C7 Lid = 13 lbs, Reclaimed Lid = 15 lbs, C6 Frame = 23 lbs, Reclaimed Frame = 33 lbs, C5 Base = 76 lbs.\n    18→*   **Fire Hydrants:**\n    19→    *   Clearances: 3' around hydrant, minimum 18\" from face of curb to steamer nozzle.\n    20→    *   Distance from ADA/pedestrian elements: Minimum 4' from ramps, strictly >6\" from any sidewalk.\n    21→    *   Hydrant Bury Depth: 4' - 5'\n    22→    *   Drainage pit: 24\" diameter and 12\" deep below the hydrant bowl.\n    23→*   **Trenching (Unfinished Surface):**\n    24→    *   Minimum cover: 300 mm (12\")\n    25→    *   Bedding envelope below pipe: 150 mm (6\")\n    26→    *   Trench width: Pipe O.D. + 300 mm (12\") minimum to Pipe O.D. + 600 mm (24\") maximum.\n    27→\n    28→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 1:** diagram — Vertical and horizontal gate valve castings. **VISION** for assembly layout and concrete block placement; **READ** for notes on stem extensions and purple/reclaimed water specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 2:** diagram — Valve riser cross-sections in full depth concrete and unpaved areas. **VISION** for spatial layout of the concrete pad and rebar; **READ** for sub-grade and paving frame requirements.\n    32→*   **Block 3 & 23:** diagram & table — Top views and sections of valve lids, frames, and boots. **VISION** for dimensions (e.g., 7 1/2\" diameter C7 lid, 9 1/4\" square reclaimed frame); **READ** Block 23 for component weights and Block 3 notes for material requirements (ASTM A48, Grade 30B).\n    33→*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n    34→*   **Block 8:** diagram — Deep water main fire hydrant installations. **VISION** for pipe configurations, 90-degree bend setups, and restraint locations.\n    35→*   **Block 5:** diagram — Typical trench detail with unfinished surface. **VISION** for the cross-section profile; **READ** for exact depth and width dimensions for the bedding envelope.\n    36→*   **Block 6:** diagram — Optional one-piece valve casting installation. **VISION** for the step-by-step visual guide to raising and lowering the riser to final grade.\n    37→*   **Blocks 7 & 9:** notes — General fire hydrant installation notes (Note: these blocks are identical). **READ** for strict spacing requirements, 24\" drainage pit specifications, 8-mil poly-film wrap instructions, and pavement marker locations.\n    38→*   **Block 10:** notes — Valve pad and delineator requirements. **READ** for required asphalt/concrete depths and instructions on placing blue/purple delineator stakes in unpaved areas.\n    39→*   **Blocks 11, 12, 13:** notes — Text extracts duplicating the notes found within the diagrams of Blocks 1, 3, and 2 respectively. **READ** only if the text in the main diagrams is illegible.\n    40→*   **Block 14:** notes — References. **READ** for standard specification manual sections (Item 510).\n    41→*   **Blocks 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the PE seal, project tracking info, and standard City of Austin title blocks (511-AW-01, 511-AW-02, 510S-5) for each standard detail. No review action needed.\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-1.md` — diagram: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n    46→- `block-3.md` — diagram: Cross-section details for valve placement in full depth concrete and unpaved areas.\n    47→- `block-9.md` — notes: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n    48→\n    49→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    50→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"7a38b6ee-f92b-4f7f-b250-06b1e1f660bc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-23/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 23 — Construction Details 2\n\nStandard construction details for water infrastructure, valves, and fire hydrants.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains \"Construction Details 2\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, specifically focusing on City of Austin standard details. It provides specifications, cross-sections, and installation procedures for typical gate valves (4\"-16\"), fire hydrant assemblies, and utility trenching with unfinished surfaces.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Gate Valves:**\n    *   Clearance: 3\" - 5\"\n    *   Concrete Block (for valves <12\"): 16\" x 16\" x 4\" minimum\n    *   Concrete cradle: Minimum 2000 P.S.I., Class B\n    *   Concrete pad patch: 3' x 3' minimum (Item 403S Class \"A\") with 5\" minimum depth and #5 rebar at mid-depth.\n    *   Total depth of asphalt + concrete: 9\" minimum\n    *   Stem extensions required when valves exceed 3' deep from finished grade; extension nut must be 12\" - 18\" from finished grade.\n    *   Valve component weights: C7 Lid = 13 lbs, Reclaimed Lid = 15 lbs, C6 Frame = 23 lbs, Reclaimed Frame = 33 lbs, C5 Base = 76 lbs.\n*   **Fire Hydrants:**\n    *   Clearances: 3' around hydrant, minimum 18\" from face of curb to steamer nozzle.\n    *   Distance from ADA/pedestrian elements: Minimum 4' from ramps, strictly >6\" from any sidewalk.\n    *   Hydrant Bury Depth: 4' - 5'\n    *   Drainage pit: 24\" diameter and 12\" deep below the hydrant bowl.\n*   **Trenching (Unfinished Surface):**\n    *   Minimum cover: 300 mm (12\")\n    *   Bedding envelope below pipe: 150 mm (6\")\n    *   Trench width: Pipe O.D. + 300 mm (12\") minimum to Pipe O.D. + 600 mm (24\") maximum.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1:** diagram — Vertical and horizontal gate valve castings. **VISION** for assembly layout and concrete block placement; **READ** for notes on stem extensions and purple/reclaimed water specifications.\n*   **Block 2:** diagram — Valve riser cross-sections in full depth concrete and unpaved areas. **VISION** for spatial layout of the concrete pad and rebar; **READ** for sub-grade and paving frame requirements.\n*   **Block 3 & 23:** diagram & table — Top views and sections of valve lids, frames, and boots. **VISION** for dimensions (e.g., 7 1/2\" diameter C7 lid, 9 1/4\" square reclaimed frame); **READ** Block 23 for component weights and Block 3 notes for material requirements (ASTM A48, Grade 30B).\n*   **Block 4:** diagram — Fire hydrant assembly plan and elevation. **VISION** for spatial clearances, layout relative to curb/sidewalks, and bottom connection options.\n*   **Block 8:** diagram — Deep water main fire hydrant installations. **VISION** for pipe configurations, 90-degree bend setups, and restraint locations.\n*   **Block 5:** diagram — Typical trench detail with unfinished surface. **VISION** for the cross-section profile; **READ** for exact depth and width dimensions for the bedding envelope.\n*   **Block 6:** diagram — Optional one-piece valve casting installation. **VISION** for the step-by-step visual guide to raising and lowering the riser to final grade.\n*   **Blocks 7 & 9:** notes — General fire hydrant installation notes (Note: these blocks are identical). **READ** for strict spacing requirements, 24\" drainage pit specifications, 8-mil poly-film wrap instructions, and pavement marker locations.\n*   **Block 10:** notes — Valve pad and delineator requirements. **READ** for required asphalt/concrete depths and instructions on placing blue/purple delineator stakes in unpaved areas.\n*   **Blocks 11, 12, 13:** notes — Text extracts duplicating the notes found within the diagrams of Blocks 1, 3, and 2 respectively. **READ** only if the text in the main diagrams is illegible.\n*   **Block 14:** notes — References. **READ** for standard specification manual sections (Item 510).\n*   **Blocks 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25:** various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the PE seal, project tracking info, and standard City of Austin title blocks (511-AW-01, 511-AW-02, 510S-5) for each standard detail. No review action needed.\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — diagram: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n- `block-3.md` — diagram: Cross-section details for valve placement in full depth concrete and unpaved areas.\n- `block-9.md` — notes: List of general notes applicable to all fire hydrant installation types.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":50}}}
