\n- EL-1.24: Streetlight poles under lines - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.25: Sidewalks cleared from poles - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.26: Trash enclosures under lines - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.28: Water meters clearance - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.29: Water lines clearance - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.30: Foundations within 5' of property line - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.32: Line crossings at 90 degrees - NEED TO CHECK (if new OHE lines)\n- EL-1.33: Secondary over primary - NEED TO CHECK (if both shown)\n- EL-1.34: Marquee signs - NOT APPLICABLE (no marquee signs)\n- EL-1.35: New power poles - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.36: Decorative lighting - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.37: Trees near lines - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.38: Meter locations obstructed - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.39: Clearances from streetlights - NEED TO CHECK (existing)\n- EL-1.40: Down guy conflicts - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.41: Guy easements transmission - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.42: Down guy easements - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.43: Transformers vertical clearance - NEED TO CHECK\n- EL-1.44: Transformers in niches - NOT APPLICABLE (no niche config shown)\n- EL-1.45: Construction staging clearances - NOT APPLICABLE (not shown in logistics detail)\n\nNeed to verify several of these items more thoroughly by reviewing the relevant drawing sheets.\n\nThe critical items to focus on are fences (EL-1.9, EL-1.10), sidewalk and pole clearances (EL-1.25), trash enclosure placement (EL-1.26), tree clearances (EL-1.37), and transformer vertical clearance (EL-1.43). I'll use vision tools to check these against the plans.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2678,"cache_read_input_tokens":74181,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2678},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa426fab-05eb-4a3a-b7ff-045b4f6362f9","uuid":"98b0