{"level":30,"time":1776273026254,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ir3bb7zyMoQDAXJMLYFpV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"0a2c1387-a718-45ca-941d-d45c6ca3d610","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776273026254,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BjehJQVm2d1GXx9ugH19KQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Electric Review section just references the Bluebeam comments link but doesn't provide the detailed comments in this document. However, it does confirm the key code references for transformer pad clearances (UCM § 1.10.4).\n\nNow let me compile my findings. Based on my comprehensive research, here's what I've found:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n### Transformer Pad Locations Identified\nThe site plan and electrical plan show 4 transformer pad locations:\n1. NW transformer (near Building 1 or 2, by main entrance)\n2. W-Central transformer (west side near Building 2)\n3. SW transformer (west side near Building 8)\n4. E Courtyard transformer (between Buildings 5, 6, 7)\n\n### Major Deficiencies Found\n\n**CRITICAL - Documentation/Dimensions Missing:**\n- No transformer pad dimensions provided on any sheet\n- No clearance measurements provided on any sheet  \n- No access door orientation shown\n- No bollard details shown\n- No AE Design-approved pad detail sheets referenced or shown\n\n**Trees/Vegetation Issues:**\n- One transformer has a callout note saying \"Tree Well need to look up approp. detail\" - tree detail is missing\n- Trees are shown near transformer pads but species identification and Appendix F utility compatibility not verified for proximity issues\n\n**Utility Separation Issues:**\n- Water, wastewater, and storm drain lines shown very close to transformer pads on Sheet 21\n- No clearance dimensions to verify 5-foot minimum separation (UCM § 2.9.1.B.2)\n- Multiple utilities (W, WW, SD) shown bracketing some pad locations\n\n**Fire Protection Issues:**\n- No fire escape locations visible on provided sheets to verify 20-foot minimum clearance (for oil-filled equipment)\n- Fire hydrant on public side, not clear if separation requirements met\n\n**Bollard/Parking Issues:**\n- No bollards shown on any sheet\n- Transformers appear to be within or very close to 4-foot proximity of circulation/parking areas\n\n\n- Without exact measurements, I can't determine if bollard protection is actually required\n\n**Access and Clearances:**\n- No hot-stick clearance areas documented (10 feet standard, 15 feet in confined space)\n- No access door orientation shown\n- No confined space analysis (niche/vault) visible\n- Grading/drainage slopes around transformers not clearly documented\n\n### NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY\n\nThe following expected elements are ABSENT from the submitted plans:\n1. AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets\n2. Transformer pad dimensions\n3. Horizontal clearance dimensions (to buildings, utilities, features)\n4. Vertical clearance demonstrations (especially for any niche or vault configurations)\n5. Access door orientations\n6. Bollard locations and details\n7. Fire rating documentation (for any reduced clearances)\n8. Tree species list cross-referenced with Appendix F for utility compatibility\n9. Root barrier details for trees within 20 feet of transformers\n10. Grading/drainage direction around oil-filled equipment pads\n11. AE Design written approval documentation (if any reduced clearances are claimed)\n\nI need to work through each checklist item to identify what's missing and what's been provided.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":74102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"473594f7-aa2f-4507-8f93-3f347d015c59"}
