],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater lines cannot be verified. Electrical plan Sheet 21 shows wastewater (WW) lines in close proximity to multiple transformer pads, particularly bracketing the northwest and west-central pads, but clearance distances are not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines cannot be verified. Electrical plan Sheet 21 shows storm drain (SD) lines parallel to transformer pad locations, but distances are not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities cannot be verified. Underground electrical lines are shown connecting to transformer pads, and multiple utilities are shown on the electrical plan, but no clearance dimensions are provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions do not match or reference Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets. No pad dimensions (length, width, depth) are shown on the electrical plan. No AE Design-approved detail sheets for the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase) are referenced or provided. Service type determination is not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations, particularly those adjacent to parking and circulation areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post (bollards) placement cannot be verified. Electrical plan shows transformer pads located within or very near circulation aisles and parking areas, but no bollard details or specifications are shown. Without dimensioned distances to parking/traffic areas and without bollard detail sheets, compliance with the 4-foot proximity requirement cannot be verified."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":74102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"087c492d-743d-44d9-825a-fc630bc759d0","uuid":"18ef9621-9de0-4bc4-8ba9-855b5ae7abdc"}
