{"level":30,"time":1776273026255,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014a2f59GKg2QyAKguyJne2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've submitted the findings. Now let me make sure I've covered all the items that should have been evaluated. Let me go through the remaining items to see if any others should be marked as not-verifiable or fail.\n\nItems I already evaluated:\n1. EL-13.1 - not-verifiable\n2. EL-13.10 - not-verifiable\n3. EL-13.13 - not-verifiable\n4. EL-13.14 - not-verifiable\n5. EL-13.21 - not-verifiable\n6. EL-13.22 - not-verifiable\n7. EL-13.23 - not-verifiable\n8. EL-13.25 - not-verifiable\n9. EL-13.37 - not-verifiable\n10. EL-13.38 - not-verifiable\n\nLet me review the remaining items:\n\n- EL-13.2: Clearances from retaining walls - Not applicable, no retaining walls adjacent to transformer pads visible from my analysis\n- EL-13.3: Clearances from fences - No fences shown near transformer pads\n- EL-13.4: Reduced 3-foot clearances with AE approval - No reduced clearances claimed or shown\n- EL-13.5: Clearances from balconies and overhangs - No balconies shown adjacent to transformer pads\n- EL-13.6: 12-foot clearance from windows/doors - Not dimensioned, but would fall under EL-13.1 which I already covered\n- EL-13.7: 2-foot clearance from sidewalks - Not dimensioned\n- EL-13.8: Stairwell clearances - Not applicable, no stairwells shown\n- EL-13.9: 20-foot clearance from fire escapes - Not verifiable (fire escapes not dimensioned relative to pads)\n\n\n- EL-13.11: 15-foot clearance for confined space - Not applicable, no niches shown\n- EL-13.12: 5-foot clearance from fire hydrants - Fire hydrants shown on site but not dimensioned relative to pads\n- EL-13.15: Root barriers - Not shown/detailed\n- EL-13.16: 5-foot clearance from dumpsters - No dumpsters shown\n- EL-13.17: 5-foot clearance from bike racks - Bike racks shown in landscape areas, not near transformers\n- EL-13.18: 5-foot clearance from light poles - Not dimensioned relative to transformer locations\n- EL-13.19: 15-foot clearance from fire lanes - Distances not provided on plans\n- EL-13.20: 5-foot clearance from other transformer pads - Multiple units present but spacing unverified\n- EL-13.24: Clearance from gas lines - No gas infrastructure indicated\n- EL-13.26: No utilities crossing over/under - Cannot confirm from available documentation\n- EL-13.27: 7.5-foot clearance from overhead lines - No overhead distribution visible on site plan\n- EL-13.28: 15-foot radius from overhead conductors - Overhead distribution not shown\n- EL-13.29: 35-foot niche clearance - No niches present\n- EL-13.30: Niche fire rating - Not required, no niches on site\n- EL-13.31: Cross-sections for vertical clearances - Not provided\n- EL-13.32: Drainage slopes for oil-filled equipment - Cannot determine transformer type from plans\n- EL-13.33: Location on private property - Transformers appear to be on private property\n- EL-13.34: Prohibited easements - Transformer placement relative to easements needs verification\n- EL-13.35: Transformer easements shown - Easements not depicted on plans\n- EL-13.36: Electrical routing 100% on private property - Requires confirmation\n- EL-13.39: Customer facilities under/over overhead distribution - No overhead distribution present on site\n\nI should reconsider which items qualify as not applicable versus not verifiable. Items like retaining walls adjacent to transformer pads would be n/a if none exist, and some clearance requirements might not apply depending on site conditions.\n\nSeveral items appear to be n/a: no retaining walls shown adjacent to pads, no fences near transformers, no reduced clearances claimed or approved, no balconies on adjacent buildings, stairwells not depicted, niches absent from plans, and dumpsters not located on site. Fire escapes are unclear since they're typically not found on multi-family townhomes with NFPA 13D sprinklers, though this needs confirmation. The private hydrant shown on site lacks dimensioning relative to the pads, making it not verifiable. Root barriers have no detail provided, and bike racks are shown but positioned away from transformers. Light poles, fire lanes, and multiple transformer pads all lack proper dimensioning. Gas lines aren't shown and only apply when service exists. Overhead lines and additional niches aren't depicted. Cross-sections are missing, and the oil-filled drainage type can't be determined from available information. The private property layout appears acceptable visually, but I need to check the prohibited easements against the actual facts.\n\nTransformer easements aren't indicated on the plans, electrical routing through private property lacks dimensions, and customer facilities under overhead lines don't apply since no overhead is shown. Reviewing more carefully, EL-13.6 regarding windows and doors within 12 feet of grade deserves separate consideration from the general setback requirements. The sidewalk clearance item shows transformers next to a planned 5-foot concrete sidewalk, but there's no dimensional verification of the required 2-foot minimum distance.\n\nLooking at the utility lines visible on the plan, water, storm drain, and wastewater lines are positioned very close to equipment pads, and transformers appear to sit within a few feet of building walls and circulation aisles. One transformer includes a tree well notation without supporting details. Several additional items warrant inclusion in the findings: windows and doors, sidewalk clearances, fire escapes, fire hydrants, root barriers, light poles, fire lanes, and other transformer pads all lack the necessary dimensions to verify compliance. Cross-sections aren't provided, oil-filled drainage equipment type isn't specified, and several other electrical