{"level":30,"time":1776273067983,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 9 and identify:\n\n1. **Fences**: Where are wood fences and other fencing shown? Do any fence posts appear to be within 10 feet of existing utility poles?\n\n2. **Sidewalks**: Where are sidewalks proposed? Are any sidewalks positioned at pole locations that would create conflicts?\n\n3. **Trash/Refuse**: Are trash receptacles or trash enclosures shown on the plan? If so, are they positioned beneath or near overhead electric lines?\n\n4. **Streetlights**: Are any new streetlight poles proposed on the site plan?\n\n5. **Water meters or electrical meters**: Are utility meters (water, sewer, electric) shown on the site? Are they positioned beneath overhead lines?\n\n6. **Transformers or other electrical equipment**: Are any transformer pads or electrical equipment shown?\n\n7. **Parking areas**: Provide details on the location and extent of parking areas relative to the overhead lines.\n\nFocus on identifying any features positioned directly beneath or in very close proximity to the overhead distribution lines marked \"- OHE -\".","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of Sheet 9 of the site plan, here are the findings regarding your requested items:\n\n**1. Fences:**\n*   A line explicitly labeled **\"Wood Fence\"** is shown running north-south along the eastern property boundary (right side of the sheet).\n*   **Proximity to Utility Poles:** At the southeast corner (bottom right of the plan), the \"Wood Fence\" line terminates at or extremely close to a circle symbol. While the word \"Pole\" is faintly visible right next to it, an \"- OHE -\" line intersects this exact point. Based on the 1\" = 20' scale, the end of this wood fence appears to be positioned immediately adjacent to (well within 10 feet of) this utility pole location. \n*   There is also a \"Fence Note\" in the bottom right corner which states: *\"Post holes that are to be installed near a trees Critical Root Zone (CRZ) will be dug by hand...\"*\n\n**2. Sidewalks:**\n*   A **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See DTL 432S-1\"** is proposed along the western boundary (left side of the sheet), running roughly parallel to the street. \n*   There are also internal walkways labeled **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"** connecting the buildings.\n*   **Conflicts with Poles:** The proposed 5' concrete sidewalk on the west runs along the same corridor as an \"- OHE -\" line. There is an \"Existing Utility Pole\" marked near the top left corner. The line denoting the proposed sidewalk appears to route past it, but it is located in very close proximity to the pole's placement along that right-of-way.\n\n**3. Trash/Refuse:**\n*   There are no large trash enclosures, dumpsters, or central refuse pads explicitly drawn or labeled on the site plan.\n*   There is a block of **\"Trash Collection Notes\"** at the bottom center of the sheet. It states: *\"Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside...\"* This suggests the use of individual roll-out bins rather than a centralized enclosure.\n\n**4. Streetlights:**\n*   There are no newly proposed streetlight poles distinctly labeled or drawn on this site plan.\n*   There is a **\"Lighting Note\"** in the bottom left corner that states: *\"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5...\"*, but it references building/site lighting rather than streetlights.\n\n**5. Water meters or electrical meters:**\n*   An **\"Existing Water Meter\"** is labeled in the far top-left corner of the drawing, near the \"Wastewater Service Connection\". \n*   No other individual utility meters (water, sewer, or electric) for the proposed units are explicitly labeled on this specific sheet. They are not shown positioned beneath the \"- OHE -\" lines.\n\n**6. Transformers or other electrical equipment:**\n*   A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is distinctly labeled on the western side of the internal site. It is located just west of a \"Tree Well,\" situated between \"Bldg. 1\" and \"Bldg. 2\".\n*   This transformer pad is located centrally within the property and is **not** positioned beneath any of the perimeter \"- OHE -\" overhead lines.\n\n**7. Parking areas:**\n*   According to the **\"Parking Data\"** table (bottom right), the site will have *\"10 Surface / 76 Garage\"* spaces. \n*   The site plan shows that the surface parking stalls and garage entrances are located centrally within the site, between and adjacent to the proposed buildings. \n*   The overhead electric lines (\"- OHE -\") run exclusively along the outer perimeters (western, southern, and eastern boundaries). Therefore, the actual parking stalls are **not** positioned beneath the overhead lines, though the entrance driveways on the south and west boundaries do cross underneath the \"- OHE -\" lines to access the public street.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1527,"outputTokens":887,"totalTokens":6074,"reasoningTokens":3660},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" 