{"level":30,"time":1776273104819,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Are there any trees (deciduous or evergreen plantings) shown on the plan near the overhead electric lines that run along the property boundaries?\n\n2. What tree species are proposed near the overhead distribution conductors (within 10 feet horizontally)?\n\n3. Are any trees shown within the utility easement areas?\n\n4. Can you identify the species names from tree callouts or legends? Do they appear to be utility-compatible species (typically marked \"UC\" in ECM Appendix F, generally mature height ≤20 feet)?\n\n5. Are there any trees shown beneath or in immediate proximity to the overhead lines marked \"- OHE -\"?\n\nThis is important for evaluating compliance with ECM § 2.4.1.D and § 2.4.2.C regarding tree placement near overhead conductors.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (labeled as Sheet \"28 of 35\" in the bottom right corner), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are there any trees (deciduous or evergreen plantings) shown on the plan near the overhead electric lines that run along the property boundaries?**\nYes. There is a line clearly marked \"-OHE-\" running horizontally along the bottom boundary of the site plan. Several tree canopy symbols are located along this boundary, and their drawn canopies intersect or are in immediate proximity to this line.\n\n**2. What tree species are proposed near the overhead distribution conductors (within 10 feet horizontally)?**\nThe specific tree species cannot be identified from this sheet. The plan uses alphanumeric callouts for trees (e.g., \"M\", \"P\", \"ST\", \"PL\"), but these do not denote plant species. Instead, text 