{"level":30,"time":1776273130514,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SpQimbmsNDuKCMAFZdwFeP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed my review of the tree clearances from overhead electric lines grouping (EL-2). Here's a summary of my findings:\n\n## Review Summary\n\n**Applicability**: This grouping IS applicable. The site has overhead electric (OHE) distribution facilities shown on the southern boundary of the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31). Trees are proposed on the landscape plan, with some positioned directly adjacent to the OHE line.\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)** - Plant species near electric facilities are not identified on the landscape plan. While the plant schedule lists all proposed species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud), there is no cross-reference showing which species are planted where, particularly for trees near the OHE facility.\n\n2. **EL-2.11 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are not differentiated on the plans. Cedar Elm and Live Oak typically mature to 40-50+ feet but are not designated as \"large trees\" on the landscape plan, and their specific locations are unknown.\n\n3. **EL-2.1 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Cannot verify species of trees within the distribution conductor clearance zone. Species identification is required to confirm utility-compatibility per ECM Appendix F.\n\n4. **EL-2.3 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Cannot verify whether large trees are within 25-foot clearance of distribution conductor due to lack of species identification and tree location specificity.\n\n5. **EL-2.14 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - While trees and overhead electric line are shown, clearance verification is prevented due to lack of species identification, distance dimensions, and detailed conductor location information.\n\n6. **EL-2.15 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - No documented Austin Energy written approval visible on submitted plans for trees proposed near overhead electric facilities. Species identification and distance verification are also required to assess this item.\n\nAll findings have been submitted in structured format. The applicant should provide:\n- Species identification for all trees on the landscape plan, particularly those near the OHE line\n- Distance dimensions from tree trunks to overhead conductors\n- Verification that species and locations comply with UCM § 1.10.10.4 requirements\n- Documentation of any required Austin Energy approvals"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2739,"cache_read_input_tokens":72136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2739},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d155abec-404b-4144-83fe-2ada3fa35846","uuid":"a81a827d-ecb4-4f76-bc99-368bb96b9726"}
