{"level":30,"time":1776273190398,"pid":22798,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":2,"prompt":"This is the Plat for Valley View Townhomes. I need to assess the property boundaries and easements in relation to transformer pad locations shown on other sheets. The three transformer locations are:\n1. Northwest - west of Bldg. 1\n2. East-Central - between Bldgs. 4-5\n3. Southwest - west of Bldg. 8\n\nPlease provide:\n1. **Property boundary location** - Where is the property line relative to these transformer locations? Are the pads on private property or near the boundary?\n2. **Easements shown on plat** - What easements are depicted? Which ones are near or affect the transformer locations?\n3. **Utility easements** - Are there electric, water, wastewater, storm drain, or other utility easements shown? What are their dimensions?\n4. **Public vs. Private areas** - Which portions of the site are dedicated easements vs. private property?\n5. **Drainage easements** - Are there drainage easements that might contain or restrict the transformer pads?\n\nThe critical requirement is UCM § 1.10.4(Table 1.10.4) footnote 4, which states transformers must be located 100% on private property and NOT in certain easements like drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines without written AE Design approval.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of the provided plat map (Sheet 2 of 39, \"MECEY SUBDIVISION\" / \"Valley View Townhomes\"), here is the detailed information regarding property boundaries, easements, and how they relate to your inquiry. \n\n**Important Context:** This sheet is a historical plat map showing the subdivision into \"LOT 1\" and \"LOT 2\". It **does not depict proposed buildings or proposed transformer pad locations.** Therefore, I must describe the boundaries and easements shown on this specific sheet so that you can cross-reference them with the sheets that *do* show the proposed transformer locations (Bldgs 1, 4-5, and 8).\n\nHere are the answers to your specific questions based solely on the visual evidence of this plat:\n\n### 1. Property Boundary Location\nThe property consists of a large roughly rectangular area divided into two tracts: \"LOT 1\" on the west and \"LOT 2\" on the east.\n*   **Western Boundary:** Fronts \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". \n    *   *Relevance to NW (west of Bldg 1) & SW (west of Bldg 8) transformers:* If these transformers are located on the western edge of the site, they will be adjacent to the Valley View Road right-of-way. They must be placed inside the solid heavy line delineating the boundary of Lot 1 to be considered on private property.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Fronts \"CLAWSON ROAD\".\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Abuts \"CORTEZ HEIGHTS - PLAT BK. 64 PG. 13\".\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Abuts \"O.R. ROGERS\" and \"BEN H. ROBERTS\".\n*   *Relevance to East-Central (between Bldgs 4-5) transformers:* Depending on the site layout, this could be near the dividing line between Lot 1 and Lot 2, or near the eastern boundary along Clawson Road.\n\n### 2. & 3. Easements Shown on Plat / Utility Easements\nThere are specific utility and drainage easements delineated by dashed lines inside the private property boundaries. \n\n*   **Along the Western Boundary (Valley View Road):**\n    *   There is a dashed line running parallel to the western property line inside Lot 1.\n    *   Text exactly as written pointing to this line (located near the southwest corner): **\"Exist. 3' Elec. Esmt.\"**\n    *   *Conflict Warning:* If the NW or SW transformers are placed within the westernmost 3 feet of the property, they will be inside this electrical easement.\n\n*   **Along the Eastern Boundary (Clawson Road):**\n    *   There is a dashed line running parallel to the eastern property line inside Lot 2.\n    *   Text exactly as written pointing to this line (located near the northeast corner): **\"3' Elec. Esm't\"**\n\n*   **Central Area (Near the boundary between Lot 1 and Lot 2):**\n    *   There is a dashed line pointing to the property line separating Lot 1 and Lot 2.\n    *   Text exactly as written: **\"10' Wastewater Line\"** \n    *   *Note:* The drawing shows a dimension of \"5'\" on the Lot 2 side of the dividing line, suggesting a 10' total easement split evenly across the lot line.\n\n### 4. Public vs. Private Areas\n*   **Private Property:** The entirety of the area inside the heavy border designated as \"LOT 1\" and \"LOT 2\" is private property. \n*   **Dedications:** The text in the upper right corner (\"THE STATE OF TEXAS COUNTY OF TRAVIS\") states: *\"...and I do hereby dedicate to the public all streets and easements as shown hereon.\"*\n*   **Conclusion:** Valley View Road and Clawson Road are public rights-of-way. The property inside the lot lines is private, but the 3' electrical, 10' wastewater, and 26' drainage areas are dedicated public utility easements located *on* private property. Per your UCM § 1.10.4 requirement, transformers must be on private property, but *cannot* be in these specific easements without written approval.\n\n### 5. Drainage Easements\nYes, there is a significant drainage easement shown.\n*   Located centrally on the site, primarily on the eastern edge of \"LOT 1\" alongside the boundary dividing it from \"LOT 2\".\n*   Text exactly as written: **\"26' Drainage Easement (Existing)\"**\n*   *Conflict Warning:* If the East-Central transformers (between Bldgs 4-5) are located near the original dividing line of these two lots, they must avoid this 26-foot drainage easement to comply with footnote 4.\n\n***\n\n### Transcribed Tables\nAs requested, here are the exact transcriptions of the tables/data blocks present on the document:\n\n**CURVE DATA**\n*(Note: 'O' represents a circle symbol with a dot in the center found on the document)*\nO\nΔ = 31°25'\nT = 20.84'\nR = 74.10'\nLC = 40.12'\nARC = 40.63'\n\n**LEGEND**\n° Iron Stake Set\n● Iron Stake Found\n*(Circle containing 'Vol', 'Page')* Travis County Deed Records\nScale 1\" = 100 Feet","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1589,"outputTokens":1184,"totalTokens":5220,"reasoningTokens":2447},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1618032]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is the Plat for Valley View Townhomes. I need to assess the property boundaries and easements in relation to transformer pad locations shown on other sheets. The three transformer locations are:\n1. Northwest - west of Bldg. 1\n2. East-Central - between Bldgs. 4-5\n3. Southwest - west of Bldg. 8\n\nPlease provide:\n1. **Property boundary location** - Where is the property line relative to these transformer locations? Are the pads on private property or near the boundary?\n2. **Easements shown on plat** - What easements are depicted? Which ones are near or affect the transformer locations?\n3. **Utility easements** - Are there electric, water, wastewater, storm drain, or other utility easements shown? What are their dimensions?\n4. **Public vs. Private areas** - Which portions of the site are dedicated easements vs. private property?\n5. **Drainage easements** - Are there drainage easements that might contain or restrict the transformer pads?\n\nThe critical requirement is UCM § 1.10.4(Table 1.10.4) footnote 4, which states transformers must be located 100% on private property and NOT in certain easements like drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements under overhead lines without written AE Design approval."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-ExDAVORKahMrxgKlVK9Ym4Ud","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Wed, 15 Apr 2026 17:13:10 GMT","server":"Vercel","set-cookie":"_vcrr_9ae7f6aec35bf5b1=dpl_DtTHaEvLxDo4bHCQosH3NskW4tQy|0.9723; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=None","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunk